ный интерфейс"],"ar":["نشر آمن للخادمات MCP","أداة ذكاء اصطناعي لتسهيل العملية","التكامل مع منصة ToolHive","دعم الخادمات MCP","واجهة مستخدم سهلة الاستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用split-pr AI工具","什么是MCP服务器","split-pr AI工具替代品","ToolHive平台教程","MCP服务器部署指南","split-pr AI工具安装","MCP服务器安全配置"],"ja":["split-pr AIエージェントの使用方法","MCPサーバーとは","split-pr AIエージェントの代替","ToolHiveプラットフォームのチュートリアル","MCPサーバーのデプロイガイド","split-pr AIエージェントのインストール","MCPサーバーのセキュリティ設定"],"ko":["split-pr AI 에이전트 사용 방법","MCP 서버란","split-pr AI 에이전트 대안","ToolHive 플랫폼 튜토리얼","MCP 서버 배포 가이드","split-pr AI 에이전트 설치","MCP 서버 보안 설정"],"es":["cómo usar split-pr","qué es split-pr","alternativas a split-pr","split-pr vs ToolHive","instalación de split-pr","guía de configuración de split-pr","herramientas de AI para servidores MCP"],"fr":["comment utiliser split-pr","quoi est split-pr","alternatives à split-pr","split-pr vs ToolHive","installation de split-pr","guide de configuration de split-pr","outils d''IA pour les serveurs MCP"],"de":["wie man split-pr verwendet","was ist split-pr","alternativen zu split-pr","split-pr vs ToolHive","installation von split-pr","konfigurationsanleitung für split-pr","KI-Tools für MCP-Server"],"pt":["como usar split-pr","o que é split-pr","ferramentas de IA para servidores MCP","split-pr vs outras ferramentas","instalar split-pr","guia de configuração do split-pr","alternativas para split-pr"],"ru":["как использовать split-pr","что такое split-pr","ИИ Агенты для серверов MCP","split-pr vs другие инструменты","установить split-pr","руководство по настройке split-pr","альтернативы для split-pr"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام split-pr","ما هو split-pr","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للخادمات MCP","split-pr مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت split-pr","دليل إعداد split-pr","بديلات لبرنامج split-pr"]}},"owner":"stacklok","repo":"toolhive","repoPath":"stacklok/toolhive","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.679Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"split-pr","description":"Analyzes current changes and suggests how to split them into smaller, reviewable PRs","bodyPreview":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for cont","body":"# Split Large PR into Smaller Changes\n\n## Purpose\n\nHelp developers break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests. This skill analyzes the current diff and proposes a splitting strategy that keeps changes atomic and reviewable.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Current Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand the scope:\n\n```bash\n# Get detailed file statistics\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat\n\n# List all changed files\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only\n\n# Show commit history for context\ngit log main...HEAD --oneline\n\n# Count non-generated files changed\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | grep -v ''zz_generated'' | grep -v ''^docs/'' | wc -l\n\n# Count lines changed (excluding generated code)\ngit diff main...HEAD --stat -- . '':(exclude)vendor/*'' '':(exclude)*.pb.go'' '':(exclude)zz_generated*'' '':(exclude)docs/*'' | tail -1\n```\n\n### 2. Evaluate Size and Complexity\n\nAssess whether the changes exceed recommended limits:\n\n- **Target limits per PR**:\n  - < 10 files changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - < 400 lines of code changed (excluding tests, generated code, docs)\n  - Changes represent one logical unit of work\n\nIf changes exceed these limits or mix multiple concerns, proceed to split analysis.\n\n### 3. Identify Logical Groupings\n\nExamine the changed files and identify natural boundaries:\n\n- **By component/package**: Group changes by the package or component they affect\n- **By layer**: Separate model changes, business logic, API changes, CLI changes\n- **By concern**: Separate refactoring from new features, bug fixes from enhancements\n- **By dependency**: Identify which changes depend on others\n\nUse these commands to help:\n\n```bash\n# Group changed files by directory\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep -v ''vendor/'' | grep -v ''\\.pb\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-2 | sort | uniq -c\n\n# Show changes by package\ngit diff main...HEAD --name-only | grep ''\\.go$'' | grep -v ''_test\\.go$'' | cut -d''/'' -f1-3 | sort | uniq -c\n```\n\n### 4. Propose Split Strategy\n\nCreate a structured plan with multiple PRs:\n\nFor each proposed PR, specify:\n- **PR Name**: Brief description (e.g., \"Add base container interface\")\n- **Purpose**: What this PR accomplishes and why it''s needed\n- **Files included**: List of files that would be in this PR\n- **Estimated size**: Approximate lines changed\n- **Dependencies**: Which other proposed PRs this depends on (if any)\n- **Test coverage**: What tests are included\n- **Order**: Suggest the sequence for creating PRs (e.g., \"Create this first\")\n\n### 5. Recommend Creation Order\n\nDetermine the optimal order for creating PRs:\n\n1. **Foundation PRs first**: New interfaces, base types, shared utilities\n2. **Refactoring PRs second**: Changes that use the new foundation\n3. **Feature PRs last**: New functionality that builds on the foundation\n4. **Independent PRs anytime**: Changes that don''t depend on others\n\n### 6. Present Action Plan\n\nProvide a clear, actionable plan:\n\n```markdown\n## Proposed PR Split\n\n### Summary\nCurrently [X] files changed with [Y] lines modified. Recommend splitting into [N] PRs:\n\n### PR 1: [Name] (Create First)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file1.go\n- path/to/file2.go\n**Size**: ~100 LOC\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Tests**: Includes unit tests for new functionality\n\n### PR 2: [Name] (After PR 1)\n**Purpose**: [What and why]\n**Files**:\n- path/to/file3.go\n**Size**: ~150 LOC\n**Dependencies**: Requires PR 1 (uses new interface)\n**Tests**: Integration tests\n\n[... continue for each PR ...]\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Would you like me to help create PR 1 first?\n2. Should I create a tracking issue for the overall work?\n3. Any changes to this split strategy?\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Splitting Principles\n\n- **Each PR should pass tests independently**: Don''t create PRs that break builds\n- **Prefer multiple small PRs over one large PR**: Easier to review and revert\n- **Keep related changes together**: Don''t artificially split code that changes together\n- **Foundation before features**: Establish abstractions before using them\n- **Use feature flags for incomplete work**: If a feature spans multiple PRs\n\n### Common Split Patterns\n\n1. **Refactoring + Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Extract interface and refactor existing code\n   - PR 2: Add new feature using the interface\n\n2. **Multi-layer Feature**:\n   - PR 1: Add data models and database changes\n   - PR 2: Add business logic layer\n   - PR 3: Add API endpoints\n   - PR 4: Add CLI commands\n\n3. **Package Restructuring**:\n   - PR 1: Create new package structure (empty or minimal)\n   - PR 2: Move code to new structure\n   - PR 3: Update imports and references\n   - PR 4: Clean up old structure\n\n4. **Kubernetes Operator Changes**:\n   - PR 1: Update CRD definitions and generate code\n   - PR 2: Update controller logic\n   - PR 3: Add validation and defaulting\n   - PR 4: Update documentation and examples\n\n### What NOT to Split\n\n- **Atomic refactorings**: Renaming that touches many files but is one logical change\n- **Generated code updates**: Proto, CRD, mock updates should stay together\n- **Dependency updates**: Keep go.mod and vendor changes in one PR\n- **Tightly coupled changes**: Changes that don''t make sense independently\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Adding New CLI Command\n\n**Current state**: 8 files changed, 450 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Add business logic to `pkg/` package (3 files, 200 lines)\n- PR 2: Add CLI command and E2E tests (5 files, 250 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Business logic is independently testable and reusable\n\n### Example 2: Refactoring + Feature\n\n**Current state**: 15 files changed, 800 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Extract common interface (2 files, 100 lines)\n- PR 2: Refactor existing implementations to use interface (6 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add new implementation with feature (7 files, 400 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR is independently valuable and testable\n\n### Example 3: Operator Enhancement\n\n**Current state**: 12 files changed, 600 lines\n\n**Split strategy**:\n- PR 1: Update CRD with new fields and generate code (4 files, 150 lines, mostly generated)\n- PR 2: Update controller to handle new fields (5 files, 300 lines)\n- PR 3: Add validation webhook (3 files, 150 lines)\n\n**Rationale**: Each PR represents a complete vertical slice of functionality\n\n## User Interaction\n\nAfter presenting the split strategy:\n\n1. **Ask for feedback**: \"Does this split make sense for your workflow?\"\n2. **Offer to adjust**: Be flexible based on user''s preferences\n3. **Help with first PR**: \"Would you like me to help create PR 1?\"\n4. **Create tracking**: \"Should I create a GitHub issue to track all PRs?\"\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Be pragmatic**: The goal is reviewable PRs, not arbitrary rules\n- **Consider the team**: Some teams prefer different split strategies\n- **Document dependencies**: Make it clear which PRs block others\n- **Test independently**: Each PR should pass CI/CD checks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:24:25.440Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing to manage large changesets with git diff and reviewable pull requests.","zh":"适合需要使用 git diff 管理大型变更集和可审查的拉取请求的代码审查代理。","ja":"大きな変更セットを git diff で管理し、レビュー可能なプルリクエストを扱うコードレビュー代理に適しています。","ko":"git diff로 대형 변경 세트를 관리하고 검토 가능한 풀 요청을 처리하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan gestionar grandes conjuntos de cambios con git diff y solicitudes de extracción revisables.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code ayant besoin de gérer de grands ensembles de modifications avec git diff et des demandes d''extraction révisables.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die große Änderungssätze mit git diff und überprüfbaren Pull-Requests verwalten müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam gerenciar grandes conjuntos de alterações com git diff e solicitações de pull revisáveis.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, которым необходимо управлять большими наборами изменений с помощью git diff и просматриваемых запросов на слияние.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات مراجعة الكود التي تحتاج إلى إدارة مجموعات كبيرة من التغييرات مع git diff وطلبات السحب القابلة للاختبار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to break down large changesets into logical, reviewable pull requests using git commands like git diff main...HEAD --stat and git diff main...HEAD --name-only, streamlining the development process with atomic and reviewable changes.","zh":"赋予代理使用 git 命令（如 git diff main...HEAD --stat 和 git diff main...HEAD --name-only）将大型变更集划分为逻辑可审查的拉取请求，简化开发过程以实现原子和可审查的更改。","ja":"エージェントに、git diff main...HEAD --statやgit diff main...HEAD --name-onlyなどのgitコマンドを使用して大きな変更セットを論理的かつレビュー可能なプルリクエストに分割する力を与え、開発プロセスを原子的かつレビュー可能な変更で簡素化します。","ko":"에이전트가 git 명령어를 사용하여(예: git diff main...HEAD --stat 및 git diff main...HEAD --name-only) 대형 변경 세트를 논리적이며 검토 가능한 풀 요청으로 분할하여 개발 프로세스를 원자적이고 검토 가능한 변경으로简化합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a descomponer grandes conjuntos de cambios en solicitudes de extracción lógicas y revisables utilizando comandos de git como git diff main...HEAD --stat y git diff main...HEAD --name-only, simplificando el proceso de desarrollo con cambios atómicos y revisables.","fr":"Permet aux agents de décomposer de grands ensembles de modifications en des demandes d''extraction logiques et révisables en utilisant des commandes git comme git diff main...HEAD --stat et git diff main...HEAD --name-only, simplifiant le processus de développement avec des modifications atomiques et révisables.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, große Änderungssätze in logische und überprüfbare Pull-Requests zu unterteilen, indem sie git-Befehle wie git diff main...HEAD --stat und git diff main...HEAD --name-only verwenden, wodurch der Entwicklungsprozess mit atomaren und überprüfbaren Änderungen gestreamt wird.","pt":"Concede poder aos agentes para dividir grandes conjuntos de alterações em solicitações de pull lógicas e revisáveis usando comandos git como git diff main...HEAD --stat e git diff main...HEAD --name-only, simplificando o processo de desenvolvimento com alterações atômicas e revisáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью разбивать большие наборы изменений на логические и просматриваемые запросы на слияние, используя команды git, такие как git diff main...HEAD --stat и git diff main...HEAD --name-only, оптимизируя процесс разработки за счет атомарных и просматриваемых изменений.","ar":"تمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تقسيم مجموعات التغييرات الكبيرة إلى طلبات سحب منطقية وقابلة للاختبار باستخدام أوامر git مثل git diff main...HEAD --stat و git diff main...HEAD --name-only، مما يبسّط عملية التطوير من خلال تغييرات ذرية وقابلة للاختبار."},"useCases":{"en":["Splitting large pull requests into smaller, reviewable changes","Analyzing current changes with git diff statistics","Proposing splitting strategies for complex changesets"],"zh":["将大型拉取请求分割为较小的可审查更改","使用 git diff 统计分析当前更改","为复杂的更改集提出分割策略"],"ja":["大きなプルリクエストを小さなレビュー可能な変更に分割する","git diff 統計で現在の変更を分析する","複雑な変更セットに分割戦略を提案する"],"ko":["대형 풀 요청을 더 작은 검토 가능한 변경으로 분할","git diff 통계를 사용하여 현재 변경 사항을 분석","복잡한 변경 세트에 대한 분할 전략을 제안"],"es":["Dividir grandes solicitudes de extracción en cambios revisables más pequeños","Analizar los cambios actuales con estadísticas de git diff","Proponer estrategias de división para conjuntos de cambios complejos"],"fr":["Diviser de grandes demandes d''extraction en des modifications révisables plus petites","Analyser les modifications actuelles avec des statistiques de git diff","Proposer des stratégies de division pour des ensembles de modifications complexes"],"de":["Große Pull-Requests in kleinere, überprüfbare Änderungen aufteilen","Aktuelle Änderungen mit git diff-Statistiken analysieren","Aufteilungsstrategien für komplexe Änderungssätze vorschlagen"],"pt":["Dividir grandes solicitações de pull em alterações menores e revisáveis","Analizar as alterações atuais com estatísticas git diff","Propor estratégias de divisão para conjuntos de alterações complexos"],"ru":["Разбить большие запросы на слияние на более мелкие и просматриваемые изменения","Анализировать текущие изменения с помощью статистики git diff","Предлагать стратегии разделения для сложных наборов изменений"],"ar":["تقسيم طلبات السحب الكبيرة إلى تغييرات صغيرة وقابلة للاختبار","تحليل التغييرات الحالية مع إحصائيات git diff","اقتراح استراتيجيات التقسيم لمجموعات التغييرات المعقدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git repository access","Limited to analyzing current diff and proposing splitting strategies"],"zh":["需要 git 存储库访问权限","仅限于分析当前 diff 并提出分割策略"],"ja":["git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","現在の diff を分析し、分割戦略を提案することのみに限定される"],"ko":["git 저장소 액세스가 필요","현재의 차이점을 분석하고 분할 전략을 제안하는 것만 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio de git","Limitado al análisis de la diferencia actual y a la propuesta de estrategias de división"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel git","Limité à l''analyse de la différence actuelle et à la proposition de stratégies de division"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das git-Repository","Begrenzt auf die Analyse der aktuellen Differenz und das Vorschlagen von Aufteilungsstrategien"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório git","Limitado à