اء الاصطناعي: open-pr لتحليل البنية التحتية","en":"open-pr"},"description":{"zh":"open-pr 是一种异步语义的架构模拟和合成技术，用于提高开发效率","ja":"open-pr は、アーキテクチャ シミュレーションと合成のための非同期セマンティクスです","ko":"open-pr 은 아키텍처 시뮬레이션과 합성을 위한 비동기 시맨틱스 기술입니다","es":"Open-pr es un agente de AI que proporciona semántica asincrónica para simulación y síntesis arquitectónica. Permite a los desarrolladores crear modelos compl...","fr":"Open-pr est un outil d''IA qui offre une sémantique asynchrone pour la simulation et la synthèse architecturale. Il permet aux développeurs de créer des modèl...","de":"Open-pr ist ein KI-Tool, das asynchrone Semantik für architektonische Simulation und Synthese bietet. Es ermöglicht Entwicklern, komplexe Modelle effizient z...","pt":"O open-pr é uma ferramenta de IA que fornece semântica assíncrona para simulação e síntese de arquitetura","ru":"ИИ Агент open-pr обеспечивает асинхронную семантику для архитектурной симуляции и синтеза","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي open-pr توفر معاني متوazenة لتحليل البنية التحتية وتوليد الكود","en":"Asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis."},"definition":{"en":"Asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis."},"features":{"zh":["异步语义技术","架构模拟和合成","提高开发效率","支持多种编程语言","易于集成和扩展"],"ja":["非同期セマンティクス","アーキテクチャ シミュレーションと合成","開発効率の向上","多くのプログラミング言語をサポート","簡単な統合と拡張"],"ko":["비동기 시맨틱스 기술","아키텍처 시뮬레이션과 합성","개발 효율성 향상","다중 프로그래밍 언어 지원","쉬운 통합과 확장"],"es":["Semántica asincrónica para simulación arquitectónica","Síntesis de modelos complejos","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Soporte para múltiples plataformas","Documentación detallada y tutoriales"],"fr":["Sémantique asynchrone pour simulation architecturale","Synthèse de modèles complexes","Intégration avec les outils de développement","Support pour plusieurs plateformes","Documentation détaillée et tutoriels"],"de":["Asynchrone Semantik für architektonische Simulation","Synthese komplexer Modelle","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Unterstützung für mehrere Plattformen","Detaillierte Dokumentation und Tutorien"],"pt":["Semântica assíncrona para simulação de arquitetura","Síntese de código para aplicações de larga escala","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento de software","Suporte a linguagens de programação como Python e Node.js","Interface de linha de comando (CLI) para automação"],"ru":["Асинхронная семантика для архитектурной симуляции","Синтез кода для крупномасштабных приложений","Интеграция с инструментами разработки программного обеспечения","Поддержка языков программирования như Python и Node.js","Интерфейс командной строки (CLI) для автоматизации"],"ar":["معاني متوazenة لتحليل البنية التحتية","توليد الكود لبرامج كبيرة الحجم","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير البرمجيات","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Python و Node.js","واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) للautomação"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 open-pr","什么是异步语义","open-pr 代替品","open-pr 安装指南","open-pr 文档","如何集成 open-pr","open-pr 和 React","open-pr 和 Python","open-pr 和 Node.js"],"ja":["open-pr の使い方","非同期セマンティクスとは","open-pr の代替品","open-pr のインストール ガイド","open-pr ドキュメント","open-pr の統合方法","open-pr と React","open-pr と Python","open-pr と Node.js"],"ko":["open-pr 사용법","비동기 시맨틱스란","open-pr 대체품","open-pr 설치 가이드","open-pr 문서","open-pr 통합 방법","open-pr 와 React","open-pr 와 Python","open-pr 와 Node.js"],"es":["cómo utilizar open-pr","qué es la semántica asincrónica","open-pr alternativa","open-pr vs otros agentes de AI","instalación de open-pr","guía de configuración de open-pr","herramientas de AI para desarrollo","simulación arquitectónica con open-pr"],"fr":["comment utiliser open-pr","qu''est-ce que la sémantique asynchrone","alternative à open-pr","open-pr vs autres outils d''IA","installation d''open-pr","guide de configuration d''open-pr","outils d''IA pour développement","simulation architecturale avec open-pr"],"de":["wie man open-pr verwendet","was ist asynchrone Semantik","Alternative zu open-pr","open-pr vs andere KI-Tools","Installation von open-pr","Konfigurationsanleitung für open-pr","KI-Tools für Entwicklung","architektonische Simulation mit open-pr"],"pt":["como usar open-pr","o que é open-pr","ferramentas de ia para simulação de arquitetura","open-pr vs outras ferramentas de ia","instalar open-pr","guia de configuração do open-pr","desenvolvimento de software com open-pr","open-pr e python","open-pr e node.js"],"ru":["как использовать open-pr","что такое open-pr","инструменты ии для архитектурной симуляции","open-pr vs другие инструменты ии","установить open-pr","руководство по настройке open-pr","разработка программного обеспечения с open-pr","open-pr и python","open-pr и node.js"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام open-pr","ما هو open-pr","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحليل البنية التحتية","open-pr مقابل أدوات أخرى للذكاء الاصطناعي","تثبيت open-pr","دليل إعداد open-pr","تطوير البرمجيات مع open-pr","open-pr و Python","open-pr و Node.js"]}},"owner":"Synthesys-Lab","repo":"assassyn","repoPath":"Synthesys-Lab/assassyn","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.680Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"open-pr","description":"Create GitHub pull requests from conversation context with proper formatting and tag selection","bodyPreview":"# Open PR\n\nThis skill instructs AI agents on how to create GitHub pull requests from conversation context\nwith meaningful titles, proper formatting, and appropriate tag selection. The AI agent\nshould analyze the conversation, extract PR details, and confirm with the user before\ncreating the pull request.\n\n## PR Format\n\nGitHub pull requests created by this skill must follow this exact structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [tag][#issue-number] Brief description of what was achieved\n\n## Summary\n\nProvide a conc","body":"# Open PR\n\nThis skill instructs AI agents on how to create GitHub pull requests from conversation context\nwith meaningful titles, proper formatting, and appropriate tag selection. The AI agent\nshould analyze the conversation, extract PR details, and confirm with the user before\ncreating the pull request.\n\n## PR Format\n\nGitHub pull requests created by this skill must follow this exact structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [tag][#issue-number] Brief description of what was achieved\n\n## Summary\n\nProvide a concise summary of what has been achieved in this PR. Focus on the\ncompleted work and the value it delivers.\n\n## Changes\n\nProvide a detailed list of changes made in this PR:\n- Modified `file_path:line_range` to implement X\n- Added `new_file.py` for Y functionality\n- Updated `config.json` to support Z\n- Removed deprecated code from `old_file.py:line_range`\n\n## Testing\n\nDescribe what was tested and how:\n- Added `tests/test_feature.py` to verify behavior A\n- Modified `tests/test_existing.py:line_range` to cover edge case B\n- Manually tested scenario C with the following steps:\n  1. Step 1\n  2. Step 2\n  3. Expected result\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #issue-number\n\n(Or \"Part of #issue-number\" if this PR partially addresses the issue)\n```\n\n## Tag Selection\n\nA `git-msg-tags.md` file should appear in `{ROOT_PROJ}/docs/git-msg-tags.md` which\ndefines the tags related to the corresponding modules or modifications. The AI agent\n**MUST** refer to this file to select the appropriate tag for the PR title.\n\nIf the file does not exist, reject the PR creation and ask the user to provide a\nlist of tags in `docs/git-msg-tags.md`.\n\n### Tag Logic\n\nThe AI agent must determine which tag to use based on the PR type by reading\n`docs/git-msg-tags.md` which contains the project''s tag definitions.\n\n**Selection guidelines:**\n- Read `docs/git-msg-tags.md` to understand available tags and their meanings\n- Choose the most specific tag that describes the primary change\n- If multiple tags could apply, choose the one that best represents the core purpose\n- If the tag is ambiguous, ask the user to select from 2-3 most relevant options\n\n## Workflow for AI Agents\n\nWhen this skill is invoked, the AI agent **MUST** follow these steps:\n\n### 1. Context Analysis Phase\n\nReview the entire conversation history and git changes to extract PR details:\n- Identify what work was completed during the conversation\n- Review git diff and git status to see actual changes made\n- Extract key details: what was changed, why, which files were affected\n- Determine the type of changes (feature, bugfix, refactor, etc.)\n- Check if there''s a related issue number mentioned in the conversation\n\nContext signals for PR type:\n- Feature signals: new functionality added, new files created, capabilities extended\n- Bugfix signals: fixed error, resolved issue, corrected behavior\n- Refactor signals: improved code structure, reorganized code, better patterns\n- Documentation signals: updated README, added comments, wrote guides\n- Test signals: added test coverage, modified test cases\n\n### 2. Git Changes Review\n\n**CRITICAL:** Before drafting the PR, the AI agent **MUST** review actual git changes:\n\n```bash\n# Check what files have changed\ngit status\n\n# Review the actual changes\ngit diff\n\n# Check commit history on current branch\ngit log origin/main..HEAD --oneline\n```\n\nThis ensures the PR description accurately reflects the actual code changes.\n\n### 3. Tag Selection Phase\n\n- Read `docs/git-msg-tags.md` to understand available tags\n- Analyze the changes and determine the primary purpose\n- Apply the tag logic described above\n- If multiple tags could apply, choose the most specific one\n- If the tag is ambiguous, ask the user to choose from 2-3 most relevant options\n\n### 4. Issue Number Extraction\n\n**CRITICAL:** The PR title **MUST** include an issue number in the format `[tag][#N]`.\n\n**How to find the issue number:**\n1. Search conversation history for explicit issue references:\n   - \"for issue #42\"\n   - \"closes #15\"\n   - \"related to #23\"\n   - GitHub issue URLs containing issue numbers\n\n2. If no issue number is found in conversation:\n   - Check if there are recent issues that match this work:\n     ```bash\n     gh issue list --limit 10\n     ```\n   - Ask the user: \"Which issue does this PR address? (Provide issue number)\"\n\n3. If user says there''s no related issue:\n   - **STOP** and inform the user:\n     ```\n     Cannot create PR without a related issue.\n     Please create an issue first using the open-issue skill, or provide an existing issue number.\n     ```\n\n**Never create a PR without an issue number.**\n\n### 5. PR Draft Construction\n\nBuild the PR following the format specification:\n\n**Title:**\n- Format: `[tag][#issue-number] Brief description`\n- The description should be in past tense (what was achieved)\n- Keep description concise (max 80 characters for the description portion)\n- Example: `[feat][#42] Add TypeScript SDK template support`\n- Example: `[bugfix][#15] Fix pre-commit hook test execution`\n\n**Summary section:**\n- Describe what has been achieved (past tense)\n- Focus on the value and purpose of the changes\n- Keep it concise but meaningful\n\n**Changes section:**\n- List specific files modified, added, or deleted\n- Include line ranges when relevant (e.g., `file.py:12-34`)\n- Describe what each change does\n- Order changes logically (not just alphabetically)\n- **DO NOT** include actual code snippets to save context length\n\n**Testing section:**\n- Describe what was tested\n- List new test files added with what they test\n- List modified test files with what new coverage was added\n- Include manual testing steps if applicable\n- Be specific about test scenarios and expected outcomes\n\n**Related Issue section:**\n- Use `Closes #N` if this PR fully resolves the issue\n- Use `Part of #N` if this PR partially addresses the issue\n- Use `Fixes #N` for bugfix PRs\n- GitHub will automatically link and close the issue when PR is merged\n\n### 6. User Confirmation Phase\n\n**CRITICAL:** The AI agent **MUST** display the complete PR draft to the user\nand wait for explicit confirmation before creating the PR.\n\nPresent the draft in a clear format:\n```\nI''ve prepared this pull request:\n\n---\n[Full PR content here]\n---\n\nShould I create this PR?\n```\n\n- Wait for explicit \"yes\", \"confirm\", \"create it\", or similar affirmative response\n- If the user requests modifications, update the draft and present again\n- If the user declines, abort PR creation gracefully\n\n### 6.5. Remote Branch Verification\n\n**CRITICAL:** Before creating the PR, verify the current branch exists on the remote repository.\n\nCheck if the current branch is tracking a remote branch:\n\n```bash\n# Check if current branch has an upstream branch\ngit rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n**If the command fails (no upstream branch):**\n1. Get the current branch name:\n   ```bash\n   git branch --show-current\n   ```\n2. Push the branch with tracking:\n   ```bash\n   git push -u origin <branch-name>\n   ```\n3. Confirm to user: \"Pushed branch to remote: origin/<branch-name>\"\n\n**If the command succeeds (upstream branch exists):**\n1. Check if local is ahead of remote:\n   ```bash\n   git status --porcelain --branch\n   ```\n2. If output contains `[ahead N]`, push changes:\n   ```bash\n   git push\n   ```\n3. If up-to-date, continue to PR creation\n\n**Error handling:**\n- If push fails due to authentication:\n  ```\n  Git push failed. Please check your Git credentials.\n  ```\n- If push fails due to conflicts:\n  ```\n  Cannot push: your branch has diverged from remote.\n  Please resolve conflicts manually with:\n    git pull --rebase origin <branch-name>\n  ```\n- For other push failures: Display the error and abort PR creation\n\n### 7. GitHub PR Creation\n\nOnce confirmed and the branch is on remote, create the PR using the GitHub CLI:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"TITLE_HERE\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nBODY_CONTENT_HERE\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n**Important:**\n- Use heredoc (`<<''EOF'' ... EOF`) to preserve markdown formatting\n- The body should include all sections from Summary onwards (not the title)\n- The PR will be created against the default branch (usually main/master)\n- After successful creation, display the PR URL to the user\n- Confirm: \"Pull request created successfully: [URL]\"\n\n**Optional flags:**\n- Add `--draft` if the user wants to create a draft PR\n- Add `--base BRANCH` if targeting a different base branch\n\n### 8. Error Handling\n\nHandle common error scenarios gracefully:\n\n**Missing git-msg-tags.md:**\n```\nCannot create PR: docs/git-msg-tags.md not found.\nPlease create this file with your project''s tag definitions.\n```\n\n**No issue number found:**\n```\nCannot create PR: No related issue number found.\n\nPlease either:\n1. Provide the issue number this PR addresses\n2. Create an issue first using the open-issue skill\n```\n\n**No git changes:**\n```\nCannot create PR: No changes detected in the working directory.\nPlease make and commit your changes first.\n```\n\n**GitHub CLI not authenticated:**\n```\nGitHub CLI is not authenticated. Please run:\n  gh auth login\n```\n\n**Not on a feature branch:**\n```\nWarning: You''re on the main/master branch.\nPRs should typically be created from feature branches.\n\nCreate a new branch with:\n  git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n\nOr confirm you want to create a PR from the current branch.\n```\n\n**No conversation context:**\n```\nI don''t have enough context to create a PR. Could you please provide:\n- What changes were made?\n- What issue does this PR address?\n- What was tested?\n```\n\n**PR creation failed:**\n```\nFailed to create pull request: [error message]\nPlease check your GitHub CLI configuration and try again.\n```\n\n## Ownership\n\nThe AI agent **SHALL NOT** claim authorship or co-authorship of the pull request.\nThe PR is created on behalf of the user, who is **FULLY** responsible for its content.\n\nDo not add any \"Created by AI\" or similar attributions to the PR body unless\nexplicitly requested by the user.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Note:** The following examples use tags like `[feat]`, `[bugfix]`, `[agent.skill]` etc.\nThese are illustrative only - actual tags must come from your project''s `docs/git-msg-tags.md`.\n\n### Example 1: Feature PR\n\n**Context:** User implemented TypeScript SDK template support to close issue #42.\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [feat][#42] Add TypeScript SDK template support\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded support for generating TypeScript SDK templates in the agentize project.\nDevelopers can now bootstrap TypeScript-based agent SDKs alongside existing\nPython templates.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Created `templates/typescript/` directory structure with standard layout\n- Added `templates/typescript/package.json` with default dependencies (typescript, @types/node)\n- Created `templates/typescript/tsconfig.json` with recommended compiler settings\n- Added `templates/typescript/src/index.ts` as the SDK entry point\n- Updated `claude/skills/sdk-init/SKILL.md` to include TypeScript as a language option\n- Modified `sdk-init` skill logic to handle TypeScript template generation\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `tests/test_typescript_template.py` to verify:\n  - Template directory creation\n  - All required files are generated correctly\n  - package.json has correct dependencies\n  - tsconfig.json has proper compiler options\n- Manually tested TypeScript template generation:\n  1. Ran sdk-init skill and selected TypeScript\n  2. Verified generated files compile without errors\n  3. Confirmed npm install works correctly\n  4. Built sample TypeScript SDK successfully\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #42\n```\n\n### Example 2: Bugfix PR\n\n**Context:** User fixed pre-commit hook not running tests (issue #15).\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [bugfix][#15] Fix pre-commit hook test execution\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed the pre-commit hook to properly execute the test suite before allowing commits.\nThe hook was not running tests due to incorrect path resolution.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Modified `.git/hooks/pre-commit:8-12` to use absolute path for test script\n- Updated hook to check exit code and block commit on test failure\n- Added error message output when tests fail\n\n## Testing\n\n- Modified `tests/test_hooks.py:23-45` to verify pre-commit hook behavior\n- Manually tested the fix:\n  1. Made changes to a Python file in `claude/skills/`\n  2. Ran `git add .` and `git commit -m \"test\"`\n  3. Confirmed tests executed and commit was blocked when tests failed\n  4. Fixed the test failure\n  5. Confirmed commit succeeded after tests passed\n\n## Related Issue\n\nFixes #15\n```\n\n### Example 3: Agent Skill PR\n\n**Context:** User created the open-pr skill (issue #67).\n\n**PR:**\n```markdown\n# [agent.skill][#67] Add open-pr skill for creating pull requests\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the open-pr skill that guides AI agents through creating well-formatted\nGitHub pull requests with proper tag selection and mandatory issue references.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Created `claude/skills/open-pr/` directory\n- Added `claude/skills/open-pr/SKILL.md` with complete PR creation workflow\n- Skill enforces issue number requirement in PR titles\n- Includes comprehensive examples and error handling guidelines\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `tests/test_open_pr_skill.py` to verify:\n  - Skill file structure and format\n  - Tag selection logic correctness\n  - Issue number extraction from various formats\n- Manually tested skill workflow:\n  1. Invoked open-pr skill in conversation\n  2. Verified it correctly extracted issue number from context\n  3. Confirmed it generated proper PR format\n  4. Tested error handling for missing issue numbers\n\n## Related Issue\n\nCloses #67\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:24:28.651Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Collaborative Agents needing automated GitHub workflow integration, particularly those utilizing Markdown formatting and asynchronous semantics for architectural simulation and synthesis.","zh":"适合需要自动化 GitHub 工作流集成的协作代理，特别是那些利用 Markdown 格式和异步语义进行架构模拟和合成的代理。","ja":"GitHub ワークフロー統合を自動化する必要があるコラボレーション エージェントに適しています。特に、Markdown 形式と非同期セマンティクスを使用したアーキテクチャのシミュレーションと合成を行うエージェントに適しています。","ko":"GitHub 워크플로 통합을 자동화해야 하는 협업 에이전트에 적합합니다. 특히 Markdown 형식 및 비동기 의미론을 사용하여 아키텍처 시뮬레이션 및 합성을 수행하는 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Colaborativos que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo de GitHub automatizado, particularmente aquellos que utilizan formato Markdown y semántica asíncrona para simulación y síntesis arquitectónica.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Collaboratifs ayant besoin d''une intégration de workflow GitHub automatisée, en particulier ceux utilisant le formatage Markdown et la sémantique asynchrone pour la simulation et la synthèse architecturale.","de":"Ideal für Kollaborationsagenten, die eine automatisierte GitHub-Workflow-Integration benötigen, insbesondere solche, die Markdown-Formatierung und asynchrone Semantik für Architektursimulation und -synthese verwenden.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Colaborativos que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho automatizada do GitHub, particularmente aqueles que utilizam formatação Markdown e semântica assíncrona para simulação e síntese arquitetônica.","ru":"Идеально для Коллаборативных Агентов, требующих автоматизированной интеграции рабочего процесса GitHub, особенно тех, которые используют форматирование Markdown и асинхронную семантику для архитектурной симуляции и синтеза.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء التعاونية التي تحتاج إلى دمج آلية العمل التلقائي على منصة GitHub، خاصة تلك التي تستخدم تنسيق Markdown والبنيات الدلالية غير المتزامنة لتحليل وتخليق الهندسة المعمارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create standardized GitHub pull requests with meaningful titles, proper formatting, and appropriate tag selection, leveraging conversation context and confirming with users before submission, all while adhering to a precise Markdown structure.","zh":"赋予代理创建标准化的 GitHub 拉取请求的能力，包括有意义的标题、适当的格式和相关标签选择，同时利用对话上下文，并在提交前确认用户，所有这些都遵循精确的 Markdown 结构。","ja":"エージェントが標準化された GitHub プルリクエストを作成できるようにし、意味のあるタイトル、適切なフォーマット、および関連するタグの選択を提供します。また、会話のコンテキストを利用し、提出前にユーザーに確認し、すべてが正確な Markdown 構造に従うようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 표준화된 GitHub 풀 요청을 생성할 수 있도록 하여 의미 있는 제목, 적절한 형식 및 관련 태그 선택을 제공하고 대화 맥락을 활용하며 제출 전에 사용자에게 확인하며 모든 것이 정확한 Markdown 구조를 따르도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear solicitudes de extracción de GitHub estandarizadas con títulos significativos, formato adecuado y selección de etiquetas apropiada, aprovechando el contexto de la conversación y confirmando con los usuarios antes de la presentación, todo mientras se adhiere a una estructura Markdown precisa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des demandes d''extraction GitHub standardisées avec des titres significatifs, un formatage approprié et une sélection de balises appropriée, en exploitant le contexte de la conversation et en confirmant avec les utilisateurs avant la soumission, tout en respectant une structure Markdown précise.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, standardisierte GitHub-Pull-Requests mit sinnvollen Titeln, ordentlichem Format und geeigneter Tag-Auswahl zu erstellen, unter Ausnutzung des Konversationskontexts und Bestätigung durch die Benutzer vor der Einreichung, während sie sich an eine präzise Markdown-Struktur halten.","pt":"Habilita agentes a criarem solicitações de pull padrão do GitHub com títulos significativos, formatação apropriada e seleção de tags adequada, aproveitando o contexto da conversa e confirmando com os usuários antes da submissão, tudo isso enquanto adere a uma estrutura Markdown precisa.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность создавать стандартизированные запросы на включение изменений в GitHub с осмысленными заголовками, правильным форматированием и соответствующим выбором тегов, используя контекст разговора и подтверждая с пользователями перед отправкой, все это при соблюдении точной структуры Markdown.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء طلبات سحب موحدة على منصة GitHub بأسماء ذات معنى وتنسيق مناسب واختيار مناسب للعلامات، مستفيدة من سياق المحادثة والتحقق مع المستخدمين قبل الإرسال، وكل ذلك مع الالتزام ببنية دقيقة من Markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pull request creation from conversation context","Generating properly formatted pull requests with relevant tags and issue numbers","Streamlining GitHub workflow through asynchronous semantics analysis"],"zh":["从对话上下文自动创建拉取请求","生成带有相关标签和问题编号的正确格式的拉取请求","通过异步语义分析简化 GitHub 工作流"],"ja":["会話のコンテキストからプルリクエストを自動的に作成する","関連するタグと問題番号を付けた適切なフォーマットのプルリクエストを生成する","非同期セマンティクスの分析を通じて GitHub ワークフローを簡素化する"],"ko":["대화 맥락에서 풀 요청을 자동으로 생성하는 것","관련 태그 및 문제 번호가 포함된 올바른 형식의 풀 요청을 생성하는 것","비동기 의미론 분석을 통해 GitHub 워크플로우를 간소화하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de solicitudes de extracción a partir del contexto de la conversación","Generación de solicitudes de extracción con formato adecuado y etiquetas relevantes y números de problema","Optimización del flujo de trabajo de GitHub a través del análisis de semántica asíncrona"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de demandes d''extraction à partir du contexte de la conversation","Génération de demandes d''extraction correctement formatées avec des balises pertinentes et des numéros de problème","Optimisation du workflow GitHub via l''analyse de la sémantique asynchrone"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Pull-Requests aus dem Konversationskontext","Erzeugung von ordentlich formatierten Pull-Requests mit relevanten Tags und Problemnummern","Optimierung des GitHub-Workflows durch Analyse asynchroner Semantik"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de solicitações de pull a partir do contexto da conversa","Gerar solicitações de pull formatadas corretamente com tags e números de issues relevantes","Otimizar o fluxo de trabalho do GitHub por meio da análise de semântica assíncrona"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание запросов на включение изменений из контекста разговора","Генерировать правильно отформатированные запросы на включение изменений с соответствующими тегами и номерами проблем","Оптимизировать рабочий процесс GitHub посредством анализа асинхронной семантики"],"ar":["تأتميت إنشاء طلبات السحب من سياق المحادثة","توليد طلبات سحب منسقة بشكل صحيح مع علامات وأرقام مشاكل ذات صلة","تحسين آلية العمل على منصة GitHub من خلال تحليل البنيات الدلالية غير المتزامنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to GitHub API","Must adhere to specific Markdown structure for pull requests","Dependent on user confirmation for pull request submission"],"zh":["需要访问 GitHub API","必须遵循特定的 Markdown 结构用于拉取请求","取决于用户确认用于拉取请求提交"],"ja":["GitHub API にアクセスする必要がある","プルリクエストには特定の Markdown 構造に従う必要がある","プルリクエストの提出にはユーザーの確認が必要である"],"ko":["GitHub API에 접근해야 함","풀 요청에는 특정 Markdown 구조를 따라야 함","풀 요청 제출은 사용자 확인에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de GitHub","Debe adherirse a una estructura Markdown específica para las solicitudes de extracción","Dependiente de la confirmación del usuario para la presentación de la solicitud de extracción"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API GitHub","Doit respecter une structure Markdown spécifique pour les demandes d''extraction","Dépend de la confirmation de l''utilisateur pour la soumission de la demande d''extraction"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die GitHub-API","Muss einer bestimmten Markdown-Struktur für Pull-Requests entsprechen","Abhängig von der Benutzerbestätigung für die Einreichung des Pull-Requests"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API do GitHub","Deve aderir a uma estrutura Markdown específica para solicitações de pull","Depende da confirmação do usuário para submissão da solicitação de pull"],"ru":["Требует доступа к API GitHub","Должно соблюдать конкретную структуру Markdown для запросов на включение изменений","Зависит от подтверждения пользователя для отправки запроса на включение изменений"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GitHub","يجب الالتزام ببنية محددة من Markdown لطلبات السحب","يعتمد على التحقق مع المستخدم لارسال طلب السحب"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3f56e2d7106c7c47364c7a2db06366c392d1c7a0b097c45eb7834aa80a9990dd","qualityScore":52}');
