フェース","AIエージェント","開発者向けツール","コマンドラインインターフェース","dexチュートリアル","dexドキュメント","jj管理"],"ko":["dex설치","dex사용법","jj터미널 인터페이스","AI 에이전트","개발자용 도구","명령줄 인터페이스","dex 튜토리얼","dex 문서","jj 관리"],"es":["dex","herramientas de AI","interfaz de terminal","jj","productividad","eficiencia","cómo usar dex","dex vs jj","instalar dex","guía de configuración de dex"],"fr":["dex","outils d''IA","interface terminale","jj","productivité","efficacité","comment utiliser dex","dex vs jj","installer dex","guide de configuration de dex"],"de":["dex","KI-Tools","Terminaloberfläche","jj","Produktivität","Effizienz","wie man dex verwendet","dex vs jj","dex installieren","dex-Konfigurationsanleitung"],"pt":["dex","ferramenta de interface terminal","jj","comandos simplificados","uso fácil"],"ru":["dex","ИИ Агент","jj","терминальный интерфейс","упрощенные команды"],"ar":["dex","أداة واجهة终端","jj","أوامر مبسطة","استخدام سهل"]}},"owner":"eliaskc","repo":"kajji","repoPath":"eliaskc/kajji","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.706Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dex","description":"Manage tasks via dex CLI. Use when breaking down complex work, tracking implementation items, or persisting context across sessions.","bodyPreview":"# Agent Coordination with dex\n\n## Command Invocation\n\nUse `dex` directly for all commands. If not on PATH, use `npx @zeeg/dex` instead.\n\n```bash\ncommand -v dex &>/dev/null && echo \"use: dex\" || echo \"use: npx @zeeg/dex\"\n```\n\n## Core Principle: Tickets, Not Todos\n\nDex tasks are **tickets** - structured artifacts with comprehensive context:\n\n- **Name**: One-line summary (issue title)\n- **Description**: Full background, requirements, approach (issue body)\n- **Result**: Implementation details, decis","body":"# Agent Coordination with dex\n\n## Command Invocation\n\nUse `dex` directly for all commands. If not on PATH, use `npx @zeeg/dex` instead.\n\n```bash\ncommand -v dex &>/dev/null && echo \"use: dex\" || echo \"use: npx @zeeg/dex\"\n```\n\n## Core Principle: Tickets, Not Todos\n\nDex tasks are **tickets** - structured artifacts with comprehensive context:\n\n- **Name**: One-line summary (issue title)\n- **Description**: Full background, requirements, approach (issue body)\n- **Result**: Implementation details, decisions, outcomes (PR description)\n\nThink: \"Would someone understand the what, why, and how from this task alone?\"\n\n## Dex Tasks are Ephemeral\n\n**Never reference dex task IDs in external artifacts** (commits, PRs, docs). Task IDs like `abc123` become meaningless once tasks are completed. Describe the work itself, not the task that tracked it.\n\n## When to Use dex\n\n**Use dex when:**\n\n- Breaking down complexity into subtasks\n- Work spans multiple sessions\n- Context needs to persist for handoffs\n- Recording decisions for future reference\n\n**Skip dex when:**\n\n- Work is a single atomic action\n- Everything fits in one session with no follow-up\n- Overhead exceeds value\n\n## dex vs Built-in Task Tools\n\nSome AI agents (like Claude Code) have built-in task tools. These are session-only and not the same as dex.\n\n|                 | dex                                   | Built-in Task Tools |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **Persistence** | Files in `.dex/`                      | Session-only        |\n| **Context**     | Rich (description + context + result) | Basic               |\n| **Hierarchy**   | 3-level (epic → task → subtask)       | Flat                |\n\nUse **dex** for persistent work. Use built-in task tools for ephemeral in-session tracking only.\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n### Create a Task\n\n```bash\ndex create \"Short name\" --description \"Full implementation context\"\n```\n\nDescription should include: what needs to be done, why, implementation approach, and acceptance criteria. See [examples.md](examples.md) for good/bad examples.\n\n### List and View Tasks\n\n```bash\ndex list                  # Pending tasks\ndex list --ready          # Unblocked tasks\ndex show <id>             # Full details\n```\n\n### Complete a Task\n\n```bash\ndex complete <id> --result \"What was accomplished\" --commit <sha>\n```\n\n**Always verify before completing.** Results must include evidence: test counts, build status, manual testing outcomes. See [verification.md](verification.md) for the full checklist.\n\n### Edit and Delete\n\n```bash\ndex edit <id> --description \"Updated description\"\ndex delete <id>\n```\n\nFor full CLI reference including blockers, see [cli-reference.md](cli-reference.md).\n\n## Understanding Task Fields\n\nTasks have two text fields:\n\n- **Name**: Brief one-line summary (shown in `dex list`)\n- **Description**: Full details - requirements, approach, acceptance criteria (shown with `--full`)\n\nWhen you run `dex show <id>`, the description may be truncated. The CLI will hint at `--full` if there''s more content.\n\n### Gathering Context\n\nWhen picking up a task, gather all relevant context:\n\n```bash\ndex show <id> --full              # Full task details\ndex show <parent-id> --full       # Parent context (if applicable)\ndex show <blocker-id> --full      # What blockers accomplished\n```\n\nBefore starting, verify you can answer:\n\n- **What** needs to be done specifically?\n- **Why** is this needed?\n- **How** should it be implemented?\n- **When** is it done (acceptance criteria)?\n\nIf any answer is unclear:\n\n1. Check parent task or completed blockers for more details\n2. Suggest entering plan mode to flesh out requirements before starting\n\n**Proceed without full context when:**\n\n- Task is trivial/atomic (e.g., \"Add .gitignore entry\")\n- Conversation already provides the missing context\n- Description itself is sufficiently detailed\n\n## Task Hierarchies\n\nThree levels: **Epic** (large initiative) → **Task** (significant work) → **Subtask** (atomic step).\n\n**Choosing the right level:**\n\n- Small feature (1-2 files) → Single task\n- Medium feature (3-7 steps) → Task with subtasks\n- Large initiative (5+ tasks) → Epic with tasks\n\n```bash\n# Create subtask under parent\ndex create --parent <id> \"Subtask name\" --description \"...\"\n```\n\nFor detailed hierarchy guidance, see [hierarchies.md](hierarchies.md).\n\n## Recording Results\n\nComplete tasks **immediately after implementing AND verifying**:\n\n- Capture decisions while fresh\n- Note deviations from plan\n- Document verification performed\n- Create follow-up tasks for tech debt\n\nYour result must include explicit verification evidence. Don''t just describe what you did—prove it works. See [verification.md](verification.md).\n\n## Commit Messages with GitHub Issues\n\nWhen a task is linked to a GitHub issue (shown in `dex show` output), include issue references in commit messages:\n\n- **Root tasks** (the task itself has GitHub metadata): Use `Fixes #N`\n  - This closes the issue when merged\n- **Subtasks** (parent/ancestor has GitHub metadata): Use `Refs #N`\n  - This links to the issue without closing it\n\nCheck `dex show <id>` for GitHub issue info before committing. The \"(via parent)\" indicator means use `Refs`, direct metadata means use `Fixes`.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Right-size tasks**: Completable in one focused session\n2. **Clear completion criteria**: Description should define \"done\"\n3. **Don''t over-decompose**: 3-7 children per parent\n4. **Action-oriented descriptions**: Start with verbs (\"Add\", \"Fix\", \"Update\")\n5. **Verify before completing**: Tests passing, manual testing done\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [cli-reference.md](cli-reference.md) - Full CLI documentation\n- [examples.md](examples.md) - Good/bad context and result examples\n- [verification.md](verification.md) - Verification checklist and process\n- [hierarchies.md](hierarchies.md) - Epic/task/subtask organization\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:42:02.214Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Task Management Agents needing structured ticketing systems with comprehensive context","zh":"非常适合需要结构化票据系统和全面上下文的任务管理代理","ja":"タスク管理エージェントが構造化されたチケットシステムと包括的なコンテキストを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"구조화된 티켓 시스템과 포괄적인 컨텍스트가 필요한 태스크 관리 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Gestión de Tareas que necesitan sistemas de ticketing estructurados con contexto integral","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion de tâches nécessitant des systèmes de ticketing structurés avec un contexte complet","de":"Perfekt für Task-Management-Agents, die strukturierte Ticketingsysteme mit umfassendem Kontext benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Tarefas que necessitam de sistemas de ticketing estruturados com contexto abrangente","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по управлению задачами, требующих структурированных систем тикетов с полным контекстом","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء لإدارة المهام الذين يحتاجون إلى أنظمة تذاكر معبأة بالسياق الشامل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage tasks as tickets with detailed names, descriptions, and results, utilizing a simple terminal interface and supporting invocation via `dex` or `npx @zeeg/dex` commands, facilitating efficient issue tracking and resolution","zh":"使代理能够使用详细的名称、描述和结果作为票据来管理任务，利用简单的终端接口，并支持通过 `dex` 或 `npx @zeeg/dex` 命令调用，促进高效的问题跟踪和解决","ja":"エージェントが詳細な名前、説明、および結果を使用してタスクをチケットとして管理できるようにし、シンプルなターミナルインターフェイスを利用し、`dex` または `npx @zeeg/dex` コマンドによる呼び出しをサポートし、効率的な問題追跡と解決を促進","ko":"에이전트가 상세한 이름, 설명 및 결과를 사용하여 태스크를 티켓으로 관리할 수 있도록 하며, 간단한 터미널 인터페이스를 활용하며, `dex` 또는 `npx @zeeg/dex` 명령어에 의한 호출을 지원하여 효율적인 문제 추적 및 해결을促進","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar tareas como tickets con nombres detallados, descripciones y resultados, utilizando una interfaz de terminal simple y soportando la invocación a través de los comandos `dex` o `npx @zeeg/dex`, facilitando el seguimiento y resolución eficientes de problemas","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des tâches comme des tickets avec des noms détaillés, des descriptions et des résultats, en utilisant une interface de terminal simple et en prenant en charge l''invocation via les commandes `dex` ou `npx @zeeg/dex`, facilitant ainsi le suivi et la résolution efficaces des problèmes","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Aufgaben als Tickets mit detaillierten Namen, Beschreibungen und Ergebnissen zu verwalten, indem sie eine einfache Terminal-Schnittstelle verwenden und die Aufruf über die Befehle `dex` oder `npx @zeeg/dex` unterstützen, wodurch eine effiziente Problemmeldung und -behebung erleichtert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar tarefas como tickets com nomes detalhados, descrições e resultados, utilizando uma interface de terminal simples e suportando invocação via comandos `dex` ou `npx @zeeg/dex`, facilitando o acompanhamento e resolução eficaz de problemas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять задачами в виде тикетов с подробными названиями, описаниями и результатами, используя простой интерфейс терминала и поддерживая вызов через команды `dex` или `npx @zeeg/dex`, что облегчает эффективное отслеживание и решение проблем","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة المهام كتذاكر مع أسماء مفصلة ووصف ونتائج، باستخدام واجهة طرفية بسيطة ودعم استدعاء عبر أوامر `dex` أو `npx @zeeg/dex`، مما يسهل تتبع القضايا وحلها بفعالية"},"useCases":{"en":["Managing project tasks with detailed issue titles and bodies","Creating and tracking tickets with comprehensive context","Invoking dex commands for streamlined task management"],"zh":["使用详细的问题标题和正文来管理项目任务","创建和跟踪具有全面上下文的票据","调用 dex 命令以实现流畅的任务管理"],"ja":["詳細な問題タイトルとボディを使用してプロジェクトタスクを管理","包括的なコンテキストを持つチケットを作成および追跡","dex コマンドを呼び出してタスク管理をストリームライン化"],"ko":["상세한 문제 제목과 본문으로 프로젝트 태스크를 관리","포괄적인 컨텍스트를 갖는 티켓을 생성 및 추적","dex 명령어를 호출하여 태스크 관리를 간소화"],"es":["Gestión de tareas de proyecto con títulos y cuerpos de problemas detallados","Creación y seguimiento de tickets con contexto integral","Invocación de comandos dex para una gestión de tareas optimizada"],"fr":["Gestion de tâches de projet avec des titres et des corps de problèmes détaillés","Création et suivi 