ficiels pour Python et Node.js pour un développement rapide","Recherche sémantique et par similarité sur les embeddings de modèles d''IA","Gestion efficace des bases de données vectorielles à l''échelle","Authentification par clé API pour un accès sécurisé","Documentation complète avec exemples de code et tutoriels"],"de":["RESTful API für einfache Integration in jeden Tech-Stack","Offizielle SDKs für Python und Node.js für schnelle Entwicklung","Semantische Suche und Ähnlichkeitssuche auf KI-Model-Embeddings","Effizientes Management von Vector Databases im großen Maßstab","API-Schlüssel-Authentifizierung für sicheren Zugriff","Umfassende Dokumentation mit Codebeispielen und Tutorials"],"pt":["Integração com VDB API","Melhoria da colaboração entre desenvolvedores","Automatização de tarefas","Suporte a múltiplos ambientes","Segurança e controle de acesso"],"ru":["Интеграция с VDB API","Улучшение сотрудничества между разработчиками","Автоматизация задач","Поддержка нескольких сред","Безопасность и контроль доступа"],"ar":["التكامل مع VDB API","تحسين التعاون بين المطورين","الآلية التلقائية للمهام","دعم بيئات متعددة","الأمان وسيطرة الوصول"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用commit-feature VDB API","什么是commit-feature","commit-feature VDB API安装","commit-feature VDB API设置指南","commit-feature VDB API替代品","commit-feature VDB API与其他工具的比较"],"ja":["commit-feature VDB APIの使い方","commit-feature VDB APIとは","commit-feature VDB APIのインストール","commit-feature VDB APIの設定ガイド","commit-feature VDB APIの代替","commit-feature VDB APIと他のツールの比較"],"ko":["commit-feature VDB API 사용 방법","commit-feature VDB API란","commit-feature VDB API 설치","commit-feature VDB API 설정 가이드","commit-feature VDB API 대체","commit-feature VDB API와 다른 도구의 비교"],"es":["commit-feature API VDB","cómo usar commit-feature","base de datos vectoriales para desarrolladores","API de embeddings AI","commit-feature install guide","commit-feature vs Pinecone","búsqueda semántica API","SDK Python VDB","Node.js vector database","integración API AI Agent"],"fr":["commit-feature API VDB","comment utiliser commit-feature","base de données vectorielle pour développeurs","API embeddings IA","guide d''installation commit-feature","commit-feature vs Pinecone","API recherche sémantique","SDK Python base vectorielle","Node.js base de données vectorielle","intégration API outil IA"],"de":["commit-feature VDB API","commit-feature如何使用","Vector Database für Entwickler","KI Embeddings API","commit-feature Installationsanleitung","commit-feature vs Pinecone","semantische Suche API","Python VDB SDK","Node.js Vektor Datenbank","KI Agenten API Integration"],"pt":["como usar commit-feature","o que é VDB API","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","commit-feature vs git","instalar commit-feature","guia de configuração do commit-feature"],"ru":["как использовать commit-feature","что такое VDB API","ИИ инструменты для разработчиков","commit-feature vs git","установить commit-feature","руководство по настройке commit-feature"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام commit-feature","ما هي VDB API","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","commit-feature vs git","تثبيت commit-feature","دليل إعداد commit-feature"]}},"owner":"Vulnetix","repo":"vdb-api","repoPath":"Vulnetix/vdb-api","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.766Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit-feature","description":"Stage changes, create conventional commit (no co-author), push to origin, and add detailed PR comment with session context","bodyPreview":"# Commit Feature Without Co-Authoring\n\nStage all changes, create a conventional commit message without Claude co-authoring, push to origin, and add a detailed PR comment with session context including TODOs and known issues.\n\n## Arguments\n\n`$ARGUMENTS` should contain:\n- **type** (required): `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `revert`\n- **scope** (optional): Component or area affected (e.g., `api`, `ui`, `auth`, `database`)\n\nExamples:\n- `/commit-fe","body":"# Commit Feature Without Co-Authoring\n\nStage all changes, create a conventional commit message without Claude co-authoring, push to origin, and add a detailed PR comment with session context including TODOs and known issues.\n\n## Arguments\n\n`$ARGUMENTS` should contain:\n- **type** (required): `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `revert`\n- **scope** (optional): Component or area affected (e.g., `api`, `ui`, `auth`, `database`)\n\nExamples:\n- `/commit-feature feat api` — New API feature\n- `/commit-feature fix validation` — Bug fix in validation\n- `/commit-feature chore deps` — Dependency updates\n\n## Step 1 — Parse Arguments\n\nExtract type and optional scope from `$ARGUMENTS`:\n\n```bash\nARGS=\"$ARGUMENTS\"\nTYPE=$(echo \"$ARGS\" | awk ''{print $1}'')\nSCOPE=$(echo \"$ARGS\" | awk ''{print $2}'')\n```\n\nValidate type is one of: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `revert`\n\nIf invalid or missing:\n```\n❌ Invalid or missing commit type\n\nUsage: /commit-feature <type> [scope]\n\nValid types:\n  feat      - New feature\n  fix       - Bug fix\n  chore     - Maintenance tasks\n  docs      - Documentation changes\n  style     - Code style/formatting\n  refactor  - Code restructuring\n  perf      - Performance improvements\n  test      - Test additions/changes\n  build     - Build system changes\n  ci        - CI/CD changes\n  revert    - Revert previous commit\n\nExample: /commit-feature feat api\n```\n\n## Step 2 — Check Git Status\n\n```bash\ngit status --porcelain\n```\n\nIf no changes found:\n```\nℹ️ No changes to commit\n\nWorking directory is clean. Make some changes first.\n```\n\n## Step 3 — Show Staged and Unstaged Changes\n\nDisplay what will be committed:\n\n```bash\necho \"📋 Files to be committed:\"\ngit status --short\n\necho \"\"\necho \"📊 Summary of changes:\"\ngit diff --stat\n```\n\n## Step 4 — Stage All Changes\n\n```bash\ngit add .\n```\n\nConfirm staging:\n```bash\ngit status --short\n```\n\n## Step 5 — Analyze Changes for Commit Message\n\nRead the git diff to understand what was changed:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --cached\n```\n\nBased on the diff, create a concise commit message following conventional commit format:\n\n**Format:**\n```\n<type>[(scope)]: <subject>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer]\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n- Subject: Imperative mood, lowercase, no period, max 50 chars\n- Body: Explain WHAT and WHY (not HOW), wrap at 72 chars\n- Footer: Breaking changes, issue references\n\n**Examples:**\n```\nfeat(api): add vulnerability triage endpoint\n\nImplements POST /api/triage for bulk finding updates with\nanalysis state, justification, and response tracking.\n\nCloses #123\n```\n\n```\nfix(validation): handle null values in SBOM parser\n\nPrevents TypeError when component.version is undefined in\nCycloneDX SBOM processing.\n```\n\n```\nchore(deps): update prisma to 5.20.0\n\nIncludes performance improvements for PostgreSQL queries\nand fixes KV cache invalidation race condition.\n```\n\n## Step 6 — Get Current Branch and PR\n\n```bash\nBRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\necho \"Current branch: $BRANCH\"\n\n# Check if PR exists\nPR_JSON=$(gh pr list --head \"$BRANCH\" --base main --json number,title,url,state --limit 1)\nPR_NUMBER=$(echo \"$PR_JSON\" | jq -r ''.[0].number // empty'')\nPR_URL=$(echo \"$PR_JSON\" | jq -r ''.[0].url // empty'')\n```\n\n## Step 7 — Create Commit (No Co-Author)\n\nCreate commit with the conventional message (WITHOUT Claude co-authoring):\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n<type>[(scope)]: <subject>\n\n<optional body>\n\n<optional footer>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT include `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` line.\n\nConfirm commit created:\n```bash\ngit log -1 --oneline\n```\n\n## Step 8 — Push to Origin\n\n```bash\ngit push origin \"$BRANCH\"\n```\n\nIf push fails (no upstream), set upstream and push:\n```bash\ngit push -u origin \"$BRANCH\"\n```\n\n## Step 9 — Collect Session Context\n\nGather detailed information for PR comment:\n\n### 9.1 — Get Session Todos\n\nUse TaskList tool to retrieve all tasks with their status, subjects, and descriptions.\n\nCategorize by status:\n- ✅ **Completed** — Tasks marked as completed\n- 🔄 **In Progress** — Tasks currently being worked on\n- ⏳ **Pending** — Tasks not yet started\n- ⚠️ **Blocked** — Tasks with unresolved blockers\n\n### 9.2 — Identify Known Issues Outside Session Scope\n\nReview the conversation history to identify:\n- Pre-existing bugs or issues mentioned but not fixed\n- Technical debt noted during implementation\n- Code patterns that should be improved later\n- Performance concerns identified but deferred\n- Security considerations for future work\n- Missing tests or documentation\n- Commented \"TODO\" or \"FIXME\" in changed files\n\nSearch for these patterns in the diff:\n```bash\ngit diff --cached | grep -E \"(TODO|FIXME|XXX|HACK|NOTE:|WARNING:)\"\n```\n\n### 9.3 — Extract Implementation Details\n\nFrom the conversation and code changes, document:\n- **Approach taken**: High-level implementation strategy\n- **Key decisions**: Why certain patterns or libraries were chosen\n- **Trade-offs**: What was prioritized and what was deferred\n- **Edge cases**: Known limitations or boundary conditions\n- **Dependencies**: New packages or services added\n- **Configuration**: Environment variables or settings changed\n\n## Step 10 — Create or Update PR Comment\n\nIf PR exists (`$PR_NUMBER` is not empty), add detailed comment:\n\n```bash\ngh pr comment \"$PR_NUMBER\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## 🤖 Session Summary\n\n### Commit Details\n**Type:** <type>\n**Scope:** <scope>\n**Message:** <commit subject>\n\n---\n\n### 📝 Implementation Context\n\n#### What Changed\n<Detailed explanation of the changes in this commit, including:>\n- Key functionality added/modified\n- Files affected and why\n- Integration points with existing code\n- Data model or API changes\n\n#### Approach & Decisions\n<Document the implementation approach:>\n- Why this solution was chosen over alternatives\n- Technical decisions made during implementation\n- Libraries or patterns introduced\n- Performance or security considerations\n\n#### Testing Notes\n<Testing considerations:>\n- Test coverage added\n- Manual testing performed\n- Edge cases validated\n- Known test gaps (if any)\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Session Tasks\n\n<If tasks exist, format as markdown checklist grouped by status>\n\n#### Completed\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n\n#### In Progress\n- [ ] Task 3\n\n#### Pending\n- [ ] Task 4\n\n<If no tasks: \"No tracked tasks for this session\">\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Known Issues & Technical Debt\n\n<List issues identified but not addressed in this commit:>\n\n#### Pre-Existing Issues\n- Issue 1: Description and why it wasn''t addressed\n- Issue 2: Description and potential impact\n\n#### Deferred Work\n- TODO 1: What needs to be done and why it was deferred\n- TODO 2: Suggested approach for future implementation\n\n#### Code Quality Notes\n- Pattern 1: Existing pattern that could be improved\n- Pattern 2: Technical debt to address in future refactor\n\n<If none: \"No significant issues identified outside session scope\">\n\n---\n\n### 🔗 Related Work\n\n<If applicable, link to:>\n- Related issues: #123, #456\n- Documentation: Link to relevant docs\n- Design docs: Link to technical design\n- Dependent PRs: #789\n\n---\n\n<Timestamp>\n📅 Generated: <current date/time>\n🤖 [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Session\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nIf NO PR exists:\n```\nℹ️ No PR found for branch ''$BRANCH''\n\nChanges committed and pushed. Create a PR with:\n  gh pr create --base main --fill\n\nThe session context can be added as a comment after PR creation.\n```\n\n## Step 11 — Final Summary\n\nOutput comprehensive summary:\n\n```\n╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n║           COMMIT & PUSH SUMMARY                   ║\n╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n\nCOMMIT:\n  Type:     <type>\n  Scope:    <scope>\n  Message:  <subject>\n  Hash:     <commit sha>\n\nBRANCH:     <branch name>\nSTATUS:     ✅ Committed and pushed\n\nFILES CHANGED:\n  Modified:   <count>\n  Added:      <count>\n  Deleted:    <count>\n\nPULL REQUEST:\n  Number:     #<pr number>\n  URL:        <pr url>\n  Comment:    ✅ Added detailed session context\n\nSESSION CONTEXT:\n  ✅ Completed tasks:     <count>\n  🔄 In progress:         <count>\n  ⏳ Pending:             <count>\n  ⚠️ Known issues:        <count>\n  📝 Implementation details included\n\nNEXT STEPS:\n  • Review PR comments for full session context\n  • Address any remaining TODOs or known issues\n  • Ensure CI/CD checks pass\n  • Request review when ready to merge\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Invalid Commit Type\n```\n❌ Invalid commit type: ''<type>''\n\nMust be one of: feat, fix, chore, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, revert\n```\n\n### No Changes to Commit\n```\nℹ️ Working directory is clean\n\nNo changes to commit. Make changes first, then run:\n  /commit-feature <type> [scope]\n```\n\n### Push Failed\n```\n❌ Failed to push to origin\n\nPossible causes:\n1. Network connectivity issues\n2. Authentication required\n3. Remote branch conflicts\n4. No upstream configured\n\nTry:\n  git push -u origin <branch>\n  # or resolve conflicts with:\n  git pull --rebase origin <branch>\n```\n\n### No PR Found\n```\nℹ️ No open PR found for branch ''<branch>''\n\nChanges committed and pushed successfully. Create PR with:\n  gh pr create --base main --fill\n\nRun /commit-feature again after PR creation to add session context.\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n```bash\n# Feature commit with scope\n/commit-feature feat api\n# → Creates: \"feat(api): add triage endpoint\"\n# → Pushes to origin\n# → Adds detailed PR comment with session context\n\n# Bug fix without scope\n/commit-feature fix\n# → Creates: \"fix: handle null values in parser\"\n# → Pushes and comments on PR\n\n# Chore with dependency scope\n/commit-feature chore deps\n# → Creates: \"chore(deps): update prisma to 5.20.0\"\n# → Documents dependency changes in PR comment\n\n# Documentation update\n/commit-feature docs\n# → Creates: \"docs: update API authentication guide\"\n# → Links to related documentation in PR comment\n```\n\n## Conventional Commit Reference\n\n| Type | Description | Example |\n|------|-------------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature | feat(auth): add OAuth2 support |\n| `fix` | Bug fix | fix(validation): prevent XSS in input |\n| `chore` | Maintenance | chore(deps): upgrade dependencies |\n| `docs` | Documentation | docs(api): update endpoint examples |\n| `style` | Formatting | style: apply prettier to codebase |\n| `refactor` | Code restructure | refactor(db): extract query helpers |\n| `perf` | Performance | perf(api): optimize database queries |\n| `test` | Tests | test(auth): add integration tests |\n| `build` | Build system | build: update webpack config |\n| `ci` | CI/CD | ci: add automated deployment |\n| `revert` | Revert commit | revert: revert \"add feature X\" |\n\n## Safety Notes\n\n- **No Claude co-authoring**: Commits will NOT include `Co-Authored-By` line\n- **Review before push**: Always verify staged changes match intent\n- **PR comments are append-only**: Multiple runs will add multiple comments\n- **Session context is detailed**: PR comments include implementation notes, TODOs, and known issues\n- **Push is automatic**: Changes will be pushed immediately after commit\n- **Conventional commits**: Follow the standard for automated changelog generation\n- **No destructive operations**: This skill only adds commits and comments\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:17:52.321Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Workflow Automation Agents handling Git repository management.","zh":"非常适合处理 Git 仓库管理的开发工作流程自动化 Agent。","ja":"Git リポジトリ管理を扱う開発ワークフロー自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Git 저장소 관리를 처리하는 개발 워크플로우 자동화 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de automatización de flujo de trabajo de desarrollo que manejan administración de repositorios Git.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation de workflow de développement gérant la gestion de référentiels Git.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklung-Workflow-Automatisierungsagenten, die Git-Repository-Verwaltung verwalten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação de Fluxo de Trabalho de Desenvolvimento que lidam com o gerenciamento de repositórios Git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов автоматизации рабочих процессов разработки, занимающихся управлением репозиториями Git.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء أتمتة سير عمل التطوير الذين يتعاملون مع إدارة مستودعات Git."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated staging, conventional commit message generation, and PR commentary with session context tracking. Provides structured argument handling for commit types and scopes while maintaining detailed development history.","zh":"支持自动暂存、生成约定式提交消息以及带有会话上下文跟踪的 PR 评论。为提交类型和范围提供结构化的参数处理，同时维护详细的开发历史记录。","ja":"自動ステージング、規約に準拠したコミットメッセージの生成、セッションコンテキストトラッキングを備えた PR コメントを可能にします。コミットタイプとスコープに対する構造化された引数処理を提供し、詳細な開発履歴を維持します。","ko":"자동 스테이징, 컨벤셔널 커밋 메시지 생성, 세션 컨텍스트 추적이 가능한 PR 코멘트 기능을 제공합니다. 커밋 유형과 범위에 대한 구조화된 인수 처리를 제공하면서도 상세한 개발 기록을 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita la automatización de la fase de prueba, la generación de mensajes de commit convencionales y los comentarios de PR con seguimiento de contexto de sesión. Proporciona el manejo de argumentos estructurados para los tipos y alcances de commit, manteniendo al mismo tiempo un historial de desarrollo detallado.","fr":"Permet l''automatisation de la phase de test, la génération de messages de commit conventionnels et les commentaires de PR avec suivi de contexte de session. Fournit la gestion d''arguments structurés pour les types et les portées de commit, tout en maintenant un historique de développement détaillé.","de":"Ermöglicht die Automatisierung der Testphase, die Generierung von konventionellen Commit-Mitteilungen und PR-Kommentaren mit Sitzungskontextnachverfolgung. Bietet strukturierte Argumentbehandlung für Commit-Typen und -Umfänge, während gleichzeitig eine detaillierte Entwicklungshistorie beibehalten wird.","pt":"Permite o staging automatizado, a geração de mensagens de commit convencionais e comentários em PR com rastreamento de contexto de sessão. Fornece manipulação estruturada de argumentos para tipos e escopos de commit, mantendo um histórico de desenvolvimento detalhado.","ru":"Обеспечивает автоматическое индексирование, создание сообщений коммитов по conventional commit и комментирование PR с отслеживанием контекста сессии. Предоставляет структурированную обработку аргументов для типов и областей коммитов, сохраняя при этом подробную историю разработки.","ar":"يمكن من التنسيق التلقائي، وإنشاء رسائل commit تقليدية، والتعليق على طلبات السحب (PR) مع تتبع سياق الجلسة. يوفر معالجة منظمة للوسيطات لأنواع commit ونطاقاتها مع الحفاظ على سجل تطوير مفصل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Git workflow standardization","Generating conventional commit messages","Tracking session context in PR comments","Staging changes without co-author dependencies"],"zh":["自动化 Git 工作流程标准化","生成约定式提交消息","在 PR 评论中跟踪会话上下文","无需协作者依赖即可暂存更改"],"ja":["Git ワークフローの標準化の自動化","規約に準拠したコミットメッセージの生成","PR コメントでのセッションコンテキストの追跡","共同作成者への依存なしでの変更のステージング"],"ko":["Git 워크플로우 표준화 자동화","컨벤셔널 커밋 메시지 생성","PR 코멘트에서 세션 컨텍스트 추적","공동 작성자 의존성 없이 변경 사항 스테이징"],"es":["Automatización de la estandarización del flujo de trabajo de Git","Generación de mensajes de commit convencionales","Seguimiento de contexto de sesión en comentarios de PR","Establecimiento de cambios sin dependencias de coautores"],"fr":["Automatisation de la standardisation du workflow Git","Génération de messages de commit conventionnels","Suivi de contexte de session dans les commentaires de PR","Mise en scène des modifications sans dépendances de coauteurs"],"de":["Automatisierung der Standardisierung des Git-Workflows","Generierung von konventionellen Commit-Mitteilungen","Nachverfolgung des Sitzungskontexts in PR-Kommentaren","Einrichtung von Änderungen ohne Co-Autoren-Abhängigkeiten"],"pt":["Automatizando a padronização do fluxo de trabalho do Git","Gerando mensagens de commit convencionais","Rastreando o contexto da sessão em comentários de PR","Preparando alterações sem dependências de co-autor"],"ru":["Автоматизация стандартизации рабочих процессов Git","Генерация сообщений коммитов по conventional commit","Отслеживание контекста сессии в комментариях PR","Индексирование изменений без зависимостей от соавторов"],"ar":["أتمتة توحيد معايير سير عمل Git","إنشاء رسائل commit تقليدية","تتبع سياق الجلسة في تعليقات طلبات السحب (PR)","تنسيق التغييرات دون الاعتماد على المؤلفين المشاركين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git repository access","Depends on conventional commit format compliance","No co-author support in commit messages"],"zh":["需要 Git 仓库访问权限","依赖于对约定式提交格式的遵守","提交消息中不支持共同作者"],"ja":["Git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","規約に準拠したコミットフォーマットへの準拠に依存","コミットメッセージでの共同作成者のサポートなし"],"ko":["Git 저장소 접근 권한 필요","컨벤셔널 커밋 형식 준수에 의존","커밋 메시지에 공동 작성자 지원 없음"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio Git","Depende del cumplimiento del formato de commit convencional","No admite coautores en los mensajes de commit"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel Git","Dépend du respect du format de commit conventionnel","N''a pas de prise en charge des coauteurs dans les messages de commit"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Git-Repository","Hängt von der Einhaltung des konventionellen Commit-Formats ab","Unterstützt keine Co-Autoren in Commit-Mitteilungen"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório Git","Depende da conformidade com o formato de commit convencional","Não há suporte a co-autor em mensagens de commit"],"ru":["Требует доступ к репозиторию Git","Зависит от соблюдения формата conventional commit","Отсутствие поддержки соавторов в сообщениях коммитов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع Git","يعتمد على الالتزام بصيغة commit التقليدية","لا يوجد دعم للمؤلفين المشاركين في رسائل commit"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7abd5bffd15cdef2c5a3514a435656ffbcecc43f498b2a981584f480b8f02852","qualityScore":52}');
