임워크","es":"Herramientas de AI: jobs-to-be-done para Agentes de IA","fr":"Outils d''IA: jobs-to-be-done pour les Agents d''IA","de":"AI-Tools: jobs-to-be-done für KI-Agents","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: jobs-to-be-done para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: jobs-to-be-done для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: jobs-to-be-done للمطورين","en":"jobs-to-be-done"},"description":{"zh":"jobs-to-be-done 技术框架是为 AI 智能代理提供的产品管理技能框架，基于 Claude Code、Cowork、Codex 等实战方法","ja":"ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ダン フレームワークは、AIエージェント向けの製品管理スキル フレームワークです。Claude Code、Cowork、Codex などの実戦方法に基づいています","ko":"jobs-to-be-done 기술 프레임워크는 AI 에이전트를 위한 제품 관리 능력 프레임워크로, Claude Code, Cowork, Codex 등의 전투 테스트된 방법에 기반","es":"El marco de habilidades de gestión de productos jobs-to-be-done está diseñado para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, Cowork, Codex","fr":"Le cadre de compétences de gestion de produits jobs-to-be-done est conçu pour les Agents d''IA tels que Claude Code, Cowork, Codex","de":"Das Produktmanagement-Skills-Framework jobs-to-be-done ist für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, Cowork, Codex konzipiert","pt":"O jobs-to-be-done é um framework de habilidades de gestão de produtos para desenvolvedores, construído com métodos testados em Claude Code, Cowork, Codex e a...","ru":"Jobs-to-be-done - это фреймворк навыков управления продуктом для разработчиков, построенный на основе проверенных методов для Claude Code, Cowork, Codex и ИИ...","ar":"jobs-to-be-done هو إطار عمل لمهارات إدارة المنتجات للمطورين، مبني على أساليب مدروسة لبرامج Claude Code و Cowork و Codex وأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي.","en":"Product Management skills framework built on battle-tested methods for Claude Code, Cowork, Codex, and AI agents."},"definition":{"en":"Product Management skills framework built on battle-tested methods for Claude Code, Cowork, Codex, and AI agents."},"features":{"zh":["基于实战方法的产品管理技能框架","支持 Claude Code、Cowork、Codex 等 AI 智能代理","高效的开发和实施","易于使用和集成","强大的扩展性和自定义性"],"ja":["実戦方法に基づく製品管理スキル フレームワーク","Claude Code、Cowork、Codex などの AIエージェントをサポート","効率的な開発と実装","使用しやすく、統合が容易","強力な拡張性とカスタマイズ性"],"ko":["전투 테스트된 방법에 기반한 제품 관리 능력 프레임워크","Claude Code, Cowork, Codex 등의 AI 에이전트 지원","효율적인 개발과 구현","사용하기 쉽고, 통합이 용이","강력한 확장성과 커스터마이징 가능"],"es":["Marco de habilidades de gestión de productos para Agentes de IA","Métodos probados para Claude Code, Cowork, Codex","Diseñado para mejorar la eficiencia y la productividad","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como React y Node.js","Compatibilidad con interfaces de línea de comandos (CLI)","Soporte para múltiples Agentes de IA"],"fr":["Cadre de compétences de gestion de produits pour les Agents d''IA","Méthodes éprouvées pour Claude Code, Cowork, Codex","Conçu pour améliorer l''efficacité et la productivité","Intégration avec des outils de développement tels que React et Node.js","Compatibilité avec les interfaces de ligne de commande (CLI)","Prise en charge de plusieurs Agents d''IA"],"de":["Produktmanagement-Skills-Framework für KI-Agents","Erprobte Methoden für Claude Code, Cowork, Codex","Konzipiert für die Verbesserung der Effizienz und Produktivität","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js","Kompatibilität mit Kommandozeilen-Schnittstellen (CLI)","Unterstützung für mehrere KI-Agents"],"pt":["Métodos de gestão de produtos testados","Integração com Claude Code, Cowork e Codex","Desenvolvido para agentes de IA","Melhoria da eficiência do desenvolvimento","Otimização do processo de gestão de produtos"],"ru":["Проверенные методы управления продуктом","Интеграция с Claude Code, Cowork и Codex","Разработано для ИИ Агентов","Улучшение эффективности разработки","Оптимизация процесса управления продуктом"],"ar":["أساليب مدروسة لإدارة المنتجات","التكامل مع برامج Claude Code و Cowork و Codex","مصمم لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين كفاءة التطوير","تحسين عملية إدارة المنتجات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","jobs-to-be-done 技术框架","产品管理技能","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","AI工具","如何使用 jobs-to-be-done","什么是 jobs-to-be-done"],"ja":["AIエージェント","ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ダン フレームワーク","製品管理スキル","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","AIツール","ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ダン の使い方","ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ダン とは"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","jobs-to-be-done 기술 프레임워크","제품 관리 능력","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","AI 도구","jobs-to-be-done 사용법","jobs-to-be-done 이란"],"es":["cómo usar jobs-to-be-done","qué es jobs-to-be-done","alternativas a jobs-to-be-done","jobs-to-be-done vs otros marcos","instalación de jobs-to-be-done","guía de configuración de jobs-to-be-done","desarrollo de Agentes de IA con jobs-to-be-done"],"fr":["comment utiliser jobs-to-be-done","qu''est-ce que jobs-to-be-done","alternatives à jobs-to-be-done","jobs-to-be-done vs autres cadres","installation de jobs-to-be-done","guide de configuration de jobs-to-be-done","développement d''Agents d''IA avec jobs-to-be-done"],"de":["wie man jobs-to-be-done verwendet","was ist jobs-to-be-done","alternativen zu jobs-to-be-done","jobs-to-be-done vs andere Frameworks","installation von jobs-to-be-done","einrichtungsanleitung für jobs-to-be-done","entwicklung von KI-Agents mit jobs-to-be-done"],"pt":["jobs-to-be-done","gestão de produtos","desenvolvimento de software","agentes de IA","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","como usar jobs-to-be-done","o que é jobs-to-be-done"],"ru":["jobs-to-be-done","управление продуктом","разработка программного обеспечения","ИИ Агенты","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","как использовать jobs-to-be-done","что такое jobs-to-be-done"],"ar":["jobs-to-be-done","إدارة المنتجات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","Claude Code","Cowork","Codex","كيفية استخدام jobs-to-be-done","ما هو jobs-to-be-done"]}},"owner":"deanpeters","repo":"Product-Manager-Skills","repoPath":"deanpeters/Product-Manager-Skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.880Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"jobs-to-be-done","description":"Systematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, vali","bodyPreview":"## Purpose\nSystematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, validate product ideas, and ensure your solution addresses real motivations—not just surface-level feature requests.\n\nThis is not a survey—it''s a structured lens for understanding *why* customers \"hire\" your product and what would make them \"fire\" it.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### The Jobs-to-be-Done","body":"## Purpose\nSystematically explore what customers are trying to accomplish (functional, social, emotional jobs), the pains they experience, and the gains they seek. Use this framework to uncover unmet needs, validate product ideas, and ensure your solution addresses real motivations—not just surface-level feature requests.\n\nThis is not a survey—it''s a structured lens for understanding *why* customers \"hire\" your product and what would make them \"fire\" it.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### The Jobs-to-be-Done Framework\nInfluenced by Clayton Christensen and the Value Proposition Canvas (Osterwalder), JTBD breaks customer needs into three categories:\n\n**1. Customer Jobs:**\n- **Functional jobs:** Tasks customers need to perform (e.g., \"send an invoice\")\n- **Social jobs:** How customers want to be perceived (e.g., \"look professional to clients\")\n- **Emotional jobs:** Emotional states customers seek or avoid (e.g., \"feel confident in my work\")\n\n**2. Pains:**\n- **Challenges:** Obstacles customers face\n- **Costliness:** What''s too expensive in time, money, or effort\n- **Common mistakes:** Errors customers make that could be prevented\n- **Unresolved problems:** Gaps in current solutions\n\n**3. Gains:**\n- **Expectations:** What would exceed current solutions\n- **Savings:** Time, money, or effort reductions that delight\n- **Adoption factors:** What increases likelihood of switching\n- **Life improvement:** How a solution makes life easier or more enjoyable\n\n### Why This Structure Works\n- **Separates job from solution:** \"Communicate with my team\" (job) ≠ \"email\" (solution)\n- **Reveals underlying motivations:** Functional job may be \"track expenses,\" but emotional job is \"feel in control of finances\"\n- **Surfaces competition you didn''t see:** Customers \"hire\" non-obvious alternatives (pen and paper, spreadsheets, workarounds)\n- **Prioritizes by intensity:** Not all pains are equal—focus on the most acute\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What This Is NOT)\n- **Not a feature wishlist:** \"I want AI, automation, and dashboards\" is not a job\n- **Not demographics:** \"Millennials want mobile-first\" is a persona trait, not a job\n- **Not generic:** \"Be more productive\" is too vague—dig into *which* tasks and *why*\n- **Not one-dimensional:** Focusing only on functional jobs misses social/emotional motivations\n\n### When to Use This\n- Early-stage discovery (before you know the solution)\n- Validating product-market fit (does your solution address the right jobs?)\n- Prioritizing roadmap (which jobs are most painful/important?)\n- Competitive analysis (what are customers \"hiring\" competitors for?)\n- Marketing messaging (speak to jobs, not features)\n\n### When NOT to Use This\n- After you''ve already built the product (too late for discovery)\n- For trivial features (don''t over-analyze small tweaks)\n- As a substitute for quantitative validation (JTBD informs hypotheses; data validates them)\n\n---\n\n## Application\n\nUse `template.md` for the full fill-in structure.\n\n### Step 1: Define the Context\nBefore exploring JTBD, clarify:\n- **Target customer segment:** Who are you studying? (reference `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`)\n- **Situation:** In what context does the job arise? (e.g., \"When managing a project deadline...\")\n- **Current solutions:** What do they use today? (competitors, workarounds, doing nothing)\n\n**If missing context:** Conduct customer interviews, contextual inquiries, or \"switch interviews\" (why they switched from a previous solution).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Explore Customer Jobs\n\n#### Functional Jobs\nAsk: \"What tasks are you trying to complete?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Functional Jobs:\n- [Task 1 customer needs to perform]\n- [Task 2 customer needs to perform]\n- [Task 3 customer needs to perform]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Reconcile monthly expenses for tax filing\"\n- \"Onboard a new team member in under 2 hours\"\n- \"Deploy code to production without downtime\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Verb-driven:** Jobs are actions (\"send,\" \"analyze,\" \"coordinate\")\n- **Solution-agnostic:** Don''t say \"use email to communicate\"—say \"communicate with remote teammates\"\n- **Specific:** \"Manage finances\" is too broad; \"Track business expenses for tax deductions\" is specific\n\n---\n\n#### Social Jobs\nAsk: \"How do you want to be perceived by others?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Social Jobs:\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 1]\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 2]\n- [Way customer wants to be perceived socially 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Be seen as a strategic thinker by my exec team\"\n- \"Appear responsive and reliable to clients\"\n- \"Look tech-savvy to my younger colleagues\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Audience-specific:** Who is the customer trying to impress? (boss, clients, peers, etc.)\n- **Emotional weight:** Social jobs often drive adoption more than functional jobs\n\n---\n\n#### Emotional Jobs\nAsk: \"What emotional state do you want to achieve or avoid?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Emotional Jobs:\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 1]\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 2]\n- [Emotional state customer seeks or avoids 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Feel confident I''m not missing important details\"\n- \"Avoid the anxiety of manual data entry errors\"\n- \"Feel a sense of accomplishment at the end of the day\"\n\n**Quality checks:**\n- **Positive and negative:** Include both what they seek (\"feel in control\") and what they avoid (\"avoid embarrassment\")\n- **Rooted in research:** Don''t fabricate emotions—use customer quotes\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Identify Pains\n\n#### Challenges\nAsk: \"What obstacles are preventing you from completing this job?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Challenges:\n- [Obstacle customer faces 1]\n- [Obstacle customer faces 2]\n- [Obstacle customer faces 3]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Tools don''t integrate, forcing manual data entry\"\n- \"No visibility into what teammates are working on\"\n- \"Approval processes take 3+ days, blocking progress\"\n\n---\n\n#### Costliness\nAsk: \"What takes too much time, money, or effort?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Costliness:\n- [What''s too costly in time, money, or effort 1]\n- [What''s too costly in time, money, or effort 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Generating monthly reports takes 8 hours of manual work\"\n- \"Hiring a specialist costs $10k, which we can''t afford\"\n- \"Learning the current tool requires 20+ hours of training\"\n\n---\n\n#### Common Mistakes\nAsk: \"What errors do you make frequently that could be prevented?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Common Mistakes:\n- [Frequent error 1]\n- [Frequent error 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Forgetting to CC stakeholders on critical emails\"\n- \"Miscalculating tax deductions due to missing receipts\"\n- \"Accidentally overwriting someone else''s work in shared files\"\n\n---\n\n#### Unresolved Problems\nAsk: \"What problems do current solutions fail to address?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Unresolved Problems:\n- [Problem not solved by current solutions 1]\n- [Problem not solved by current solutions 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Current CRM doesn''t track customer health scores\"\n- \"Email doesn''t preserve conversation context when people are added mid-thread\"\n- \"Existing tools require technical expertise we don''t have\"\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Uncover Gains\n\n#### Expectations\nAsk: \"What would make you love a solution?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Expectations:\n- [What could exceed expectations 1]\n- [What could exceed expectations 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Automatically categorizes expenses without manual tagging\"\n- \"Suggests next steps based on project status\"\n- \"Integrates seamlessly with tools we already use\"\n\n---\n\n#### Savings\nAsk: \"What savings in time, money, or effort would delight you?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Savings:\n- [Way of saving time, money, or effort 1]\n- [Way of saving time, money, or effort 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Reduce report generation from 8 hours to 10 minutes\"\n- \"Eliminate the need for a full-time admin\"\n- \"Cut onboarding time from 2 weeks to 2 days\"\n\n---\n\n#### Adoption Factors\nAsk: \"What would make you switch from your current solution?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Adoption Factors:\n- [Factor increasing likelihood of adoption 1]\n- [Factor increasing likelihood of adoption 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"Free trial with no credit card required\"\n- \"Migration support to import existing data\"\n- \"Testimonials from companies like ours\"\n\n---\n\n#### Life Improvement\nAsk: \"How would your life be better if this job were easier?\"\n\n```markdown\n### Life Improvement:\n- [How solution makes life easier or more enjoyable 1]\n- [How solution makes life easier or more enjoyable 2]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n- \"I could leave work on time instead of staying late to finish reports\"\n- \"I''d feel less stressed about missing important deadlines\"\n- \"I could focus on strategic work instead of busywork\"\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Prioritize and Validate\n\n- **Rank pains by intensity:** Which pains are acute vs. mild annoyances?\n- **Identify must-have vs. nice-to-have gains:** What would drive adoption vs. what''s just a bonus?\n- **Cross-reference with personas:** Do different personas have different jobs/pains/gains? (reference `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`)\n- **Validate with data:** Survey a broader audience to confirm JTBD insights from interviews\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `examples/sample.md` for full JTBD examples.\n\nMini example excerpt:\n\n```markdown\n**Functional Jobs:** Coordinate tasks across a distributed team\n**Pains - Challenges:** Team members use different tools, creating silos\n**Gains - Savings:** Reduce status reporting time from 3 hours to 15 minutes\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### Pitfall 1: Confusing Jobs with Solutions\n**Symptom:** \"I need to use Slack\" or \"I need AI-powered analytics\"\n\n**Consequence:** You''ve anchored on a solution, not the underlying job.\n\n**Fix:** Ask \"Why?\" 5 times. \"I need Slack\" → \"Why?\" → \"To communicate with my team\" → \"Why?\" → \"To get quick answers\" → \"Why?\" → \"To avoid project delays.\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 2: Generic Jobs\n**Symptom:** \"Be more productive\" or \"Save time\"\n\n**Consequence:** Too vague to inform product decisions.\n\n**Fix:** Get specific. \"Save time\" → \"Reduce time spent generating monthly reports from 8 hours to 1 hour.\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 3: Ignoring Social/Emotional Jobs\n**Symptom:** Only documenting functional jobs\n\n**Consequence:** You miss powerful motivators. People often buy based on emotional/social needs, not just functional.\n\n**Fix:** Explicitly ask about perception and emotions in interviews. \"How would solving this make you feel?\" \"Who would notice if you solved this?\"\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 4: Fabricating JTBD Without Research\n**Symptom:** Filling out the template based on assumptions\n\n**Consequence:** You''re guessing. JTBD analysis is only valuable if grounded in real customer insights.\n\n**Fix:** Conduct \"switch interviews\" (ask why they switched from a previous solution), contextual inquiries, or problem validation interviews.\n\n---\n\n### Pitfall 5: Treating All Pains as Equal\n**Symptom:** Listing 20 pains without prioritization\n\n**Consequence:** No clarity on what to solve first.\n\n**Fix:** Rank pains by intensity (acute vs. mild). Ask \"If we only solved one pain, which would have the biggest impact?\"\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### Related Skills\n- `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md` — Defines who has these jobs/pains/gains\n- `skills/problem-statement/SKILL.md` — JTBD informs the \"Trying to\" and \"But\" sections\n- `skills/positioning-statement/SKILL.md` — JTBD informs the \"that need\" statement\n\n### External Frameworks\n- Clayton Christensen, *Competing Against Luck* (2016) — Origin of Jobs-to-be-Done theory\n- Tony Ulwick, *Outcome-Driven Innovation* (2016) — Quantifying jobs and outcomes\n- Alexander Osterwalder, *Value Proposition Canvas* (2014) — Customer jobs/pains/gains framework\n\n### Dean''s Work\n- [Link to relevant Dean Peters'' Substack articles if applicable]\n\n### Provenance\n- Adapted from `prompts/jobs-to-be-done.md` in the `https://github.com/deanpeters/product-manager-prompts` repo.\n\n---\n\n**Skill type:** Component\n**Suggested filename:** `jobs-to-be-done.md`\n**Suggested placement:** `/skills/components/`\n**Dependencies:** References `skills/proto-persona/SKILL.md`\n**Used by:** `skills/positioning-statement/SKILL.md`, `skills/problem-statement/SKILL.md`, `skills/epic-hypothesis/SKILL.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:53:01.315Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Product Management Agents needing customer-centric product development capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要以客户为中心的产品开发能力的产品管理代理","ja":"顧客中心の製品開発機能を必要とする製品管理エージェントに最適","ko":"고객 중심의 제품 개발 능력이 필요한 제품 관리 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Gestión de Productos que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo de productos centrados en el cliente.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion de produits ayant besoin de capacités de développement de produits axées sur le client.","de":"Perfekt für Produktmanagement-Agenten, die kundenorientierte Produktentwicklungs-Fähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gestão de Produtos que necessitam de capacidades de desenvolvimento de produtos centradas no cliente.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по управлению продуктами, которым необходимы возможности разработки продуктов, ориентированных на клиентов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة المنتج التي تحتاج إلى قدرات تطوير المنتجات المتمحورة حول العملاء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically explore customer motivations, uncover unmet needs, and validate product ideas using a jobs-to-be-done framework, leveraging functional, social, and emotional job analysis to inform product decisions.","zh":"赋予代理商系统地探索客户动机、揭示未满足的需求、并使用工作框架验证产品理念，利用功能性、社会性和情感性工作分析来指导产品决策","ja":"エージェントが顧客の動機を体系的に探求し、満たされていないニーズを発見し、ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ドゥーン・フレームワークを使用して製品アイデアを検証することを可能にし、機能的、社会的、感情的なジョブ分析を使用して製品の決定を情報に基づくものにする","ko":"에이전트가 고객의 동기를 체계적으로 탐색하고 미충족된 요구를 발견하며 작업 프레임워크를 사용하여 제품 아이디어를 검증할 수 있도록 하며, 기능적, 사회적, 감정적 작업 분석을 사용하여 제품 결정에 정보를 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a explorar sistemáticamente las motivaciones de los clientes, descubrir necesidades insatisfechas y validar ideas de productos utilizando un marco de trabajo de jobs-to-be-done, aprovechando el análisis de trabajo funcional, social y emocional para informar decisiones de producto.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''explorer systématiquement les motivations des clients, de découvrir des besoins non satisfaits et de valider des idées de produits en utilisant un cadre de travail de jobs-to-be-done, en exploitant l''analyse de travail fonctionnel, social et émotionnel pour éclairer les décisions de produit.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Motivationen der Kunden systematisch zu erkunden, unerfüllte Bedürfnisse aufzudecken und Produktideen unter Verwendung eines jobs-to-be-done-Frameworks zu validieren, das funktionale, soziale und emotionale Jobanalyse nutzt, um Produktentscheidungen zu informieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a explorar sistematicamente as motivações dos clientes, descobrir necessidades não atendidas e validar ideias de produtos usando uma estrutura de trabalhos a serem feitos, aproveitando a análise de trabalho funcional, social e emocional para informar decisões de produtos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически исследовать мотивацию клиентов, выявлять неудовлетворенные потребности и проверять идеи продуктов с использованием рамок задач, которые необходимо выполнить, используя функциональный, социальный и эмоциональный анализ работы для информирования решений по продуктам.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من استكشاف دوافع العملاء بشكل منهجي، وكشف الاحتياجات غير الملباة، واعتماد أفكار المنتجات باستخدام إطار للوظائف التي يجب القيام بها، واستخدام تحليل الوظيفة الوظيفية والاجتماعية والعاطفية لإبلاغ قرارات المنتج."},"useCases":{"en":["Uncovering unmet customer needs through functional job analysis","Validating product ideas against customer motivations and pain points","Informing product development with emotional and social job analysis"],"zh":["通过功能性工作分析揭示未满足的客户需求","验证产品理念是否符合客户动机和痛点","使用情感性和社会性工作分析来指导产品开发"],"ja":["機能的ジョブ分析を通じて満たされていない顧客ニーズを発見する","顧客の動機と痛点に対する製品アイデアを検証する","感情的および社会的ジョブ分析を使用して製品開発に情報を提供する"],"ko":["기능적 작업 분석을 통해 미충족된 고객 요구를 발견","고객의 동기와 고통 点에 대한 제품 아이디어를 검증","감정적 및 사회적 작업 분석을 사용하여 제품 개발에 정보를 제공"],"es":["Descubrir necesidades insatisfechas de los clientes a través del análisis de trabajo funcional","Validar ideas de productos frente a motivaciones y puntos de dolor de los clientes","Informar el desarrollo de productos con análisis de trabajo emocional y social"],"fr":["Découvrir les besoins non satisfaits des clients grâce à l''analyse de travail fonctionnel","Valider les idées de produits par rapport aux motivations et aux points de douleur des clients","Informer le développement de produits avec l''analyse de travail émotionnel et social"],"de":["Aufdecken unerfüllter Kundenbedürfnisse durch funktionale Jobanalyse","Validieren von Produktideen gegenüber Kundenmotivationen und Schmerzpunkten","Informieren der Produktentwicklung mit emotionaler und sozialer Jobanalyse"],"pt":["Descobrir necessidades não atendidas dos clientes por meio da análise de trabalho funcional","Validar ideias de produtos contra motivações e pontos de dor dos clientes","Informar o desenvolvimento de produtos com análise de trabalho emocional e social"],"ru":["Выявление неудовлетворенных потребностей клиентов посредством функционального анализа работы","Проверка идей продуктов на соответствие мотивациям и болевым точкам клиентов","Информирование разработки продуктов с помощью эмоционального и социального анализа работы"],"ar":["كشف الاحتياجات غير الملباة للعملاء من خلال تحليل الوظيفة الوظيفية","اعتماد أفكار المنتجات مقابل دوافع العملاء ونقاط الألم","إبلاغ تطوير المنتجات بالتحليل العاطفي والاجتماعي للوظيفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive customer data and feedback","May necessitate iterative product refinement based on jobs-to-be-done insights"],"zh":["需要全面性的客户数据和反馈","可能需要根据工作框架的见解进行迭代的产品改进"],"ja":["包括的な顧客データとフィードバックが必要","ジョブズ・トゥ・ビー・ドゥーン・フレームワークの洞察に基づいて製品の反復改良が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["포괄적인 고객 데이터와 피드백이 필요","작업 프레임워크의 통찰에 따라 제품의 반복적 개선이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere datos y comentarios de clientes exhaustivos","Puede necesitar un perfeccionamiento iterativo del producto basado en los conocimientos de jobs-to-be-done"],"fr":["Nécessite des données et des commentaires clients complets","Peut nécessiter un raffinement itératif du produit basé sur les connaissances de jobs-to-be-done"],"de":["Benötigt umfassende Kunden-Daten und -Feedback","Kann eine iterative Produktverfeinerung auf Basis von jobs-to-be-done-Erkenntnissen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige dados e feedback abrangentes do cliente","Pode necessitar de refinamento iterativo do produto com base em insights de trabalhos a serem feitos"],"ru":["Требует всесторонних данных и обратной связи от клиента","Может потребовать итеративного усовершенствования продукта на основе выводов из рамок задач, которые необходимо выполнить"],"ar":["يتطلب بيانات واعترادات شاملة من العميل","يمكن أن يتطلب تعديلاً متكرراً للمنتج بناءً على رؤى الوظائف التي يجب القيام بها"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"f9e48392089be00bc9005d74bf0778654170cb4ce21f6bba462a54b1da40ab7f","qualityScore":51}');
