ntas de AI para desarrolladores","mejora de la calidad del código con AI"],"fr":["comment utiliser les outils d''IA","qu''est-ce qu''un agent IA","agents IA pour Go","alternatives aux agents IA","installation des outils d''IA","guide de configuration des agents IA","développement de logiciels avec IA","outils d''IA pour les développeurs","amélioration de la qualité du code avec IA"],"de":["wie man AI-Tools verwendet","was ist ein AI-Agent","AI-Agents für Go","Alternativen zu AI-Agents","Installation von AI-Tools","Konfigurationsanleitung für AI-Agents","Software-Entwicklung mit AI","AI-Tools für Entwickler","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität mit AI"],"pt":["go-functional-options","código Go idiômático","desenvolvimento de software","produtividade em desenvolvimento","escalabilidade em Go","ferramentas de desenvolvimento Go","guia de instalação go-functional-options","configuração go-functional-options"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты go-functional-options","идиоматический код Go","разработка программного обеспечения","производительность в разработке","масштабируемость в Go","инструменты разработки Go","руководство по установке go-functional-options","настройка go-functional-options"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي go-functional-options","كود Go بالشكل المثالي","تطوير البرمجيات","الإنتاجية في التطوير","الAMERA في Go","أدوات التطوير Go","دليل تثبيت go-functional-options","إعداد go-functional-options"]}},"owner":"cxuu","repo":"golang-skills","repoPath":"cxuu/golang-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.960Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"go-functional-options","description":"The functional options pattern for Go constructors and public APIs. Use when designing APIs with optional configuration, especially with 3+ parameters.","bodyPreview":"# Functional Options Pattern\n\n> **Source**: Uber Go Style Guide\n\nFunctional options is a pattern where you declare an opaque `Option` type that records information in an internal struct. The constructor accepts a variadic number of these options and applies them to configure the result.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse functional options when:\n\n- **3+ optional arguments** on constructors or public APIs\n- **Extensible APIs** that may gain new options over time\n- **Clean caller experience** is important (no n","body":"# Functional Options Pattern\n\n> **Source**: Uber Go Style Guide\n\nFunctional options is a pattern where you declare an opaque `Option` type that records information in an internal struct. The constructor accepts a variadic number of these options and applies them to configure the result.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse functional options when:\n\n- **3+ optional arguments** on constructors or public APIs\n- **Extensible APIs** that may gain new options over time\n- **Clean caller experience** is important (no need to pass defaults)\n\n## The Pattern\n\n### Core Components\n\n1. **Unexported `options` struct** - holds all configuration\n2. **Exported `Option` interface** - with unexported `apply` method\n3. **Option types** - implement the interface\n4. **`With*` constructors** - create options\n\n### Option Interface\n\n```go\ntype Option interface {\n    apply(*options)\n}\n```\n\nThe unexported `apply` method ensures only options from this package can be used.\n\n## Complete Implementation\n\n> **Source**: Uber Go Style Guide\n\n```go\npackage db\n\nimport \"go.uber.org/zap\"\n\n// options holds all configuration for opening a connection.\ntype options struct {\n    cache  bool\n    logger *zap.Logger\n}\n\n// Option configures how we open the connection.\ntype Option interface {\n    apply(*options)\n}\n\n// cacheOption implements Option for cache setting (simple type alias).\ntype cacheOption bool\n\nfunc (c cacheOption) apply(opts *options) {\n    opts.cache = bool(c)\n}\n\n// WithCache enables or disables caching.\nfunc WithCache(c bool) Option {\n    return cacheOption(c)\n}\n\n// loggerOption implements Option for logger setting (struct for pointers).\ntype loggerOption struct {\n    Log *zap.Logger\n}\n\nfunc (l loggerOption) apply(opts *options) {\n    opts.logger = l.Log\n}\n\n// WithLogger sets the logger for the connection.\nfunc WithLogger(log *zap.Logger) Option {\n    return loggerOption{Log: log}\n}\n\n// Open creates a connection.\nfunc Open(addr string, opts ...Option) (*Connection, error) {\n    // Start with defaults\n    options := options{\n        cache:  defaultCache,\n        logger: zap.NewNop(),\n    }\n\n    // Apply all provided options\n    for _, o := range opts {\n        o.apply(&options)\n    }\n\n    // Use options.cache and options.logger...\n    return &Connection{}, nil\n}\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n> **Source**: Uber Go Style Guide\n\n### Without Functional Options (Bad)\n\n```go\n// Caller must always provide all parameters, even defaults\ndb.Open(addr, db.DefaultCache, zap.NewNop())\ndb.Open(addr, db.DefaultCache, log)\ndb.Open(addr, false /* cache */, zap.NewNop())\ndb.Open(addr, false /* cache */, log)\n```\n\n### With Functional Options (Good)\n\n```go\n// Only provide options when needed\ndb.Open(addr)\ndb.Open(addr, db.WithLogger(log))\ndb.Open(addr, db.WithCache(false))\ndb.Open(\n    addr,\n    db.WithCache(false),\n    db.WithLogger(log),\n)\n```\n\n## Comparison: Functional Options vs Config Struct\n\n| Aspect | Functional Options | Config Struct |\n|--------|-------------------|---------------|\n| **Extensibility** | Add new `With*` functions | Add new fields (may break) |\n| **Defaults** | Built into constructor | Zero values or separate defaults |\n| **Caller experience** | Only specify what differs | Must construct entire struct |\n| **Testability** | Options are comparable | Struct comparison |\n| **Complexity** | More boilerplate | Simpler setup |\n\n**Prefer Config Struct when**: Fewer than 3 options, options rarely change, all options usually specified together, or internal APIs only.\n\n## Why Not Closures?\n\n> **Source**: Uber Go Style Guide\n\nAn alternative implementation uses closures:\n\n```go\n// Closure approach (not recommended)\ntype Option func(*options)\n\nfunc WithCache(c bool) Option {\n    return func(o *options) { o.cache = c }\n}\n```\n\nThe interface approach is preferred because:\n\n1. **Testability** - Options can be compared in tests and mocks\n2. **Debuggability** - Options can implement `fmt.Stringer`\n3. **Flexibility** - Options can implement additional interfaces\n4. **Visibility** - Option types are visible in documentation\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```go\n// 1. Unexported options struct with defaults\ntype options struct {\n    field1 Type1\n    field2 Type2\n}\n\n// 2. Exported Option interface, unexported method\ntype Option interface {\n    apply(*options)\n}\n\n// 3. Option type + apply + With* constructor\ntype field1Option Type1\n\nfunc (o field1Option) apply(opts *options) { opts.field1 = Type1(o) }\nfunc WithField1(v Type1) Option            { return field1Option(v) }\n\n// 4. Constructor applies options over defaults\nfunc New(required string, opts ...Option) (*Thing, error) {\n    o := options{field1: defaultField1, field2: defaultField2}\n    for _, opt := range opts {\n        opt.apply(&o)\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [ ] `options` struct is unexported\n- [ ] `Option` interface has unexported `apply` method\n- [ ] Each option has a `With*` constructor\n- [ ] Defaults are set before applying options\n- [ ] Required parameters are separate from `...Option`\n\n## See Also\n\n- `go-style-core` - Core Go style principles\n- `go-naming` - Naming conventions for Go\n- `go-defensive` - Defensive programming patterns\n- [Self-referential functions and the design of options](https://commandcenter.blogspot.com/2014/01/self-referential-functions-and-design.html) - Rob Pike\n- [Functional options for friendly APIs](https://dave.cheney.net/2014/10/17/functional-options-for-friendly-apis) - Dave Cheney\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:13:35.780Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Go-based AI Agents requiring flexible and extensible configuration options with the Functional Options Pattern","zh":"适用于需要灵活和可扩展配置选项的Go-based AI Agents，采用函数选项模式","ja":"GoベースのAIエージェントに適しており、関数オプションパターンを使用して柔軟で拡張可能な構成オプションを提供する","ko":"유연하고 확장 가능한 구성 옵션을 필요로 하는 Go 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 함수 옵션 패턴을 사용합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial basados en Go que requieren opciones de configuración flexibles y extensibles con el patrón de opciones funcionales","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle basés sur Go nécessitant des options de configuration flexibles et extensibles avec le modèle d''options fonctionnelles","de":"Ideal für auf Go basierende KI-Agents, die flexible und erweiterbare Konfigurationsoptionen mit dem Muster der Funktionsoptionen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA baseados em Go que exigem opções de configuração flexíveis e extensíveis com o Padrão de Opções Funcionais","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ на основе Go, требующих гибких и расширяемых вариантов конфигурации с помощью шаблона функциональных опций","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوكيل الذكي المبني على Go الذي يتطلب خيارات تكوين مرنة وقابلة للتوسيع باستخدام نمط الخيارات الوظيفية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to configure Go applications using an opaque Option type, enabling clean caller experiences and extensible APIs with variadic optional arguments, following Uber''s Go Style Guide for idiomatic code","zh":"赋予代理使用不透明的选项类型配置Go应用程序的能力，实现清晰的调用者体验和可扩展的API，具有可变的可选参数，遵循Uber的Go风格指南以实现成语代码","ja":"エージェントが不透明なオプションタイプを使用してGoアプリケーションを構成し、クリーンなコール者体験と可変のオプション引数を使用した拡張可能なAPIを実現する力を与え、UberのGoスタイルガイドに従って成語コードを作成する","ko":"에이전트가 불투명한 옵션 유형을 사용하여 Go 애플리케이션을 구성하고, 깨끗한 호출자 경험과 가변 옵션 인수를 사용하는 확장 가능한 API를 제공하는 기능을 부여하며, Uber의 Go 스타일 가이드에 따라 관용적 코드를 작성합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a configurar aplicaciones Go mediante un tipo de opción opaco, lo que permite experiencias de llamador limpias y API extensibles con argumentos opcionales variádicos, siguiendo la Guía de estilo de Go de Uber para código idiomático","fr":"Permet aux agents de configurer des applications Go à l''aide d''un type d''option opaque, permettant ainsi des expériences d''appelant propres et des API extensibles avec des arguments facultatifs variadiques, en suivant le Guide de style Go d''Uber pour un code idiomatique","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Go-Anwendungen mithilfe eines undurchsichtigen Optionstyps zu konfigurieren, wodurch saubere Aufrufererfahrungen und erweiterbare APIs mit variadischen optionalen Argumenten ermöglicht werden, wobei der Go-Style-Guide von Uber für idiomatischen Code befolgt wird","pt":"Habilita agentes a configurar aplicativos Go usando um tipo de Opção opaco, permitindo experiências de chamador limpas e APIs extensíveis com argumentos opcionais variádicos, seguindo o Guia de Estilo Go da Uber para código idiomático","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью конфигурировать приложения Go с помощью непрозрачных опций, обеспечивая чистые вызовы и расширяемые API с переменным количеством необязательных аргументов, следуя Руководству по стилю Go от Uber для идиоматического кода","ar":"يمكّن الوكيل من تكوين تطبيقات Go باستخدام نوع خيار غير شفاف، وتمكين تجارب المتصلين النظيفة وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات القابلة للتوسيع مع حجج اختيارية متغيرة، اتباع دليل أسلوب Go من Uber للرمز المتعارف عليه"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing functional options for constructors with 3+ optional arguments","Designing extensible APIs that may gain new options over time","Enhancing caller experience with clean and flexible configuration options"],"zh":["为构造函数实现具有3个以上可选参数的函数选项","设计可能随时间获得新选项的可扩展API","通过清晰和灵活的配置选项增强调用者体验"],"ja":["3つ以上のオプション引数を持つコンストラクタのための関数オプションを実装する","新しいオプションを取得する可能性のある拡張可能なAPIを設計する","クリーンで柔軟な構成オプションを使用してコール者体験を強化する"],"ko":["3개 이상의 선택적 인수를 가진 생성자의 함수 옵션을 구현하는 것","새로운 옵션을 얻을 수 있는 확장 가능한 API를 설계하는 것","깨끗하고 유연한 구성 옵션을 사용하여 호출자 경험을 향상시키는 것"],"es":["Implementar opciones funcionales para constructores con 3+ argumentos opcionales","Diseñar API extensibles que 