guration de cursor"],"de":["KI-Agent-Tools","KI-Framework","wie man KI-Agents verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu Claude Code","Installationsanleitung für Codex","Cursor-Konfiguration"],"pt":["como usar start framework","AI Agents TypeScript","CLI para desenvolvimento IA","start vs cursor comparison","instalar start framework","workflow automação coding","ferramentas developer AI","setup start typescript"],"ru":["как использовать start фреймворк","ИИ Агенты TypeScript","CLI для разработки ИИ","start vs cursor сравнение","установить start framework","workflow автоматизация кодирования","инструменты developer AI","настройка start typescript"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام إطار عمل start","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي TypeScript","واجهة سطر أوامر لتطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","مقارنة start مقابل cursor","تثبيت إطار عمل start","أتمتة سير عمل البرمجة","أدوات مطوري الذكاء الاصطناعي","إعداد start typescript"]}},"owner":"mindfold-ai","repo":"Trellis","repoPath":"mindfold-ai/Trellis","stars":2875,"forks":149,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T01:53:07Z","topics":["ai-agent","ai-coding","claude-code","cli","codex","cursor","developer-tools","typescript","workflow"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"start","description":"Start Session","bodyPreview":"# Start Session\n\nInitialize your AI development session and begin working on tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Operation Types\n\n| Marker | Meaning | Executor |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| `[AI]` | Bash scripts or tool calls executed by AI | You (AI) |\n| `[USER]` | Skills executed by user | User |\n\n---\n\n## Initialization `[AI]`\n\n### Step 1: Understand Development Workflow\n\nFirst, read the workflow guide to understand the development process:\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/workflow.md\n```\n\n**Follow the instructions in","body":"# Start Session\n\nInitialize your AI development session and begin working on tasks.\n\n---\n\n## Operation Types\n\n| Marker | Meaning | Executor |\n|--------|---------|----------|\n| `[AI]` | Bash scripts or tool calls executed by AI | You (AI) |\n| `[USER]` | Skills executed by user | User |\n\n---\n\n## Initialization `[AI]`\n\n### Step 1: Understand Development Workflow\n\nFirst, read the workflow guide to understand the development process:\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/workflow.md\n```\n\n**Follow the instructions in workflow.md** - it contains:\n- Core principles (Read Before Write, Follow Standards, etc.)\n- File system structure\n- Development process\n- Best practices\n\n### Step 2: Get Current Context\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py\n```\n\nThis shows: developer identity, git status, current task (if any), active tasks.\n\n### Step 3: Read Guidelines Index\n\n```bash\ncat .trellis/spec/frontend/index.md  # Frontend guidelines\ncat .trellis/spec/backend/index.md   # Backend guidelines\ncat .trellis/spec/guides/index.md    # Thinking guides\n```\n\n### Step 4: Report and Ask\n\nReport what you learned and ask: \"What would you like to work on?\"\n\n---\n\n## Task Classification\n\nWhen user describes a task, classify it:\n\n| Type | Criteria | Workflow |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| **Question** | User asks about code, architecture, or how something works | Answer directly |\n| **Trivial Fix** | Typo fix, comment update, single-line change, < 5 minutes | Direct Edit |\n| **Simple Task** | Clear goal, 1-2 files, well-defined scope | Quick confirm → Task Workflow |\n| **Complex Task** | Vague goal, multiple files, architectural decisions | **Brainstorm → Task Workflow** |\n\n### Decision Rule\n\n> **If in doubt, use Brainstorm + Task Workflow.**\n>\n> Task Workflow ensures code-specs are injected to the right context, resulting in higher quality code.\n> The overhead is minimal, but the benefit is significant.\n\n---\n\n## Question / Trivial Fix\n\nFor questions or trivial fixes, work directly:\n\n1. Answer question or make the fix\n2. If code was changed, remind user to run `$finish-work`\n\n---\n\n## Simple Task\n\nFor simple, well-defined tasks:\n\n1. Quick confirm: \"I understand you want to [goal]. Ready to proceed?\"\n2. If yes, proceed to **Task Workflow Phase 1 Path B** (create task, write PRD, then research)\n3. If no, clarify and confirm again\n\n---\n\n## Complex Task - Brainstorm First\n\nFor complex or vague tasks, use the brainstorm process to clarify requirements.\n\nSee `$brainstorm` for the full process. Summary:\n\n1. **Acknowledge and classify** - State your understanding\n2. **Create task directory** - Track evolving requirements in `prd.md`\n3. **Ask questions one at a time** - Update PRD after each answer\n4. **Propose approaches** - For architectural decisions\n5. **Confirm final requirements** - Get explicit approval\n6. **Proceed to Task Workflow** - With clear requirements in PRD\n\n---\n\n## Task Workflow (Development Tasks)\n\n**Why this workflow?**\n- Run a dedicated research pass before coding\n- Configure specs in jsonl context files\n- Implement using injected context\n- Verify with a separate check pass\n- Result: Code that follows project conventions automatically\n\n### Overview: Two Entry Points\n\n```\nFrom Brainstorm (Complex Task):\n  PRD confirmed → Research → Configure Context → Activate → Implement → Check → Complete\n\nFrom Simple Task:\n  Confirm → Create Task → Write PRD → Research → Configure Context → Activate → Implement → Check → Complete\n```\n\n**Key principle: Research happens AFTER requirements are clear (PRD exists).**\n\n---\n\n### Phase 1: Establish Requirements\n\n#### Path A: From Brainstorm (skip to Phase 2)\n\nPRD and task directory already exist from brainstorm. Skip directly to Phase 2.\n\n#### Path B: From Simple Task\n\n**Step 1: Confirm Understanding** `[AI]`\n\nQuick confirm:\n- What is the goal?\n- What type of development? (frontend / backend / fullstack)\n- Any specific requirements or constraints?\n\nIf unclear, ask clarifying questions.\n\n**Step 2: Create Task Directory** `[AI]`\n\n```bash\nTASK_DIR=$(python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create \"<title>\" --slug <name>)\n```\n\n**Step 3: Write PRD** `[AI]`\n\nCreate `prd.md` in the task directory with:\n\n```markdown\n# <Task Title>\n\n## Goal\n<What we''re trying to achieve>\n\n## Requirements\n- <Requirement 1>\n- <Requirement 2>\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] <Criterion 1>\n- [ ] <Criterion 2>\n\n## Technical Notes\n<Any technical decisions or constraints>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Prepare for Implementation (shared)\n\n> Both paths converge here. PRD and task directory must exist before proceeding.\n\n**Step 4: Code-Spec Depth Check** `[AI]`\n\nIf the task touches infra or cross-layer contracts, do not start implementation until code-spec depth is defined.\n\nTrigger this requirement when the change includes any of:\n- New or changed command/API signatures\n- Database schema or migration changes\n- Infra integrations (storage, queue, cache, secrets, env contracts)\n- Cross-layer payload transformations\n\nMust-have before proceeding:\n- [ ] Target code-spec files to update are identified\n- [ ] Concrete contract is defined (signature, fields, env keys)\n- [ ] Validation and error matrix is defined\n- [ ] At least one Good/Base/Bad case is defined\n\n**Step 5: Research the Codebase** `[AI]`\n\nBased on the confirmed PRD, run a focused research pass and produce:\n\n1. Relevant spec files in `.trellis/spec/`\n2. Existing code patterns to follow (2-3 examples)\n3. Files that will likely need modification\n\nUse this output format:\n\n```markdown\n## Relevant Specs\n- <path>: <why it''s relevant>\n\n## Code Patterns Found\n- <pattern>: <example file path>\n\n## Files to Modify\n- <path>: <what change>\n```\n\n**Step 6: Configure Context** `[AI]`\n\nInitialize default context:\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py init-context \"$TASK_DIR\" <type>\n# type: backend | frontend | fullstack\n```\n\nAdd specs found in your research pass:\n\n```bash\n# For each relevant spec and code pattern:\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context \"$TASK_DIR\" implement \"<path>\" \"<reason>\"\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context \"$TASK_DIR\" check \"<path>\" \"<reason>\"\n```\n\n**Step 7: Activate Task** `[AI]`\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start \"$TASK_DIR\"\n```\n\nThis sets `.current-task` so hooks can inject context.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Execute (shared)\n\n**Step 8: Implement** `[AI]`\n\nImplement the task described in `prd.md`.\n\n- Follow all specs injected into implement context\n- Keep changes scoped to requirements\n- Run lint and typecheck before finishing\n\n**Step 9: Check Quality** `[AI]`\n\nRun a quality pass against check context:\n\n- Review all code changes against the specs\n- Fix issues directly\n- Ensure lint and typecheck pass\n\n**Step 10: Complete** `[AI]`\n\n1. Verify lint and typecheck pass\n2. Report what was implemented\n3. Remind user to:\n   - Test the changes\n   - Commit when ready\n   - Run `$record-session` to record this session\n\n---\n\n## Continuing Existing Task\n\nIf `get_context.py` shows a current task:\n\n1. Read the task''s `prd.md` to understand the goal\n2. Check `task.json` for current status and phase\n3. Ask user: \"Continue working on <task-name>?\"\n\nIf yes, resume from the appropriate step (usually Step 7 or 8).\n\n---\n\n## Skills Reference\n\n### User Skills `[USER]`\n\n| Skill | When to Use |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `$start` | Begin a session (this skill) |\n| `$finish-work` | Before committing changes |\n| `$record-session` | After completing a task |\n\n### AI Scripts `[AI]`\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py` | Get session context |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py create` | Create task directory |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py init-context` | Initialize jsonl files |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py add-context` | Add spec to jsonl |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start` | Set current task |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py finish` | Clear current task |\n| `python3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py archive` | Archive completed task |\n\n### Workflow Phases `[AI]`\n\n| Phase | Purpose | Context Source |\n|-------|---------|----------------|\n| research | Analyze codebase | direct repo inspection |\n| implement | Write code | `implement.jsonl` |\n| check | Review & fix | `check.jsonl` |\n| debug | Fix specific issues | `debug.jsonl` |\n\n---\n\n## Key Principle\n\n> **Code-spec context is injected, not remembered.**\n>\n> The Task Workflow ensures agents receive relevant code-spec context automatically.\n> This is more reliable than hoping the AI \"remembers\" conventions.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T02:13:34.759Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing streamlined workflow initialization and task management.","zh":"非常适合需要简化工作流初始化和任务管理的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントがワークフローの初期化とタスク管理を効率化する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 워크플로우 초기화와 작업 관리를 간소화해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una inicialización de flujo de trabajo y gestión de tareas simplificadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une initialisation de workflow et une gestion de tâches rationalisées.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine gestreamte Workflow-Initialisierung und Aufgabenverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de inicialização de fluxo de trabalho simplificado e gerenciamento de tarefas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима упрощенная инициализация рабочего процесса и управление задачами.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تهيئة تدفق العمل المُبسطة وتحكم المهام."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize development sessions, execute Bash scripts, and interact with workflow guides using Markdown files, providing a comprehensive development framework.","zh":"赋予代理初始化开发会话、执行Bash脚本和使用Markdown文件与工作流指南交互的能力，提供了一个全面的开发框架。","ja":"開発エージェントが開発セッションを初期化し、Bashスクリプトを実行し、Markdownファイルを使用してワークフローガイドとやり取りできるようにし、包括的な開発フレームワークを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 개발 세션을 초기화하고 Bash 스크립트를 실행하며 Markdown 파일을 사용하여 워크플로우 가이드와 상호 작용할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 종합적인 개발 프레임워크를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar sesiones de desarrollo, ejecutar scripts de Bash y interactuar con guías de flujo de trabajo utilizando archivos Markdown, proporcionando un marco de desarrollo integral que incluye React, Python, CLI y API.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''initialiser des sessions de développement, d''exécuter des scripts Bash et d''interagir avec des guides de workflow à l''aide de fichiers Markdown, fournissant un cadre de développement complet qui inclut React, Python, CLI et API.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Entwicklungssitzungen zu initialisieren, Bash-Skripte auszuführen und mit Workflow-Leitfäden über Markdown-Dateien zu interagieren, wodurch ein umfassendes Entwicklungsframework bereitgestellt wird, das React, Python, CLI und API umfasst.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar sessões de desenvolvimento, executar scripts Bash e interagir com guias de fluxo de trabalho usando arquivos Markdown, fornecendo uma estrutura de desenvolvimento abrangente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью инициализации сессий разработки, выполнения скриптов Bash и взаимодействия с рабочими руководствами с использованием файлов Markdown, обеспечивая комплексную разработочную структуру.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تهيئة جلسات التطوير وتشغيل سكريبتات Bash والتفاعل مع دلائل التدفق العمل باستخدام ملفات Markdown، مما يوفر إطارًا شاملاً للتنمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing AI development sessions","Executing Bash scripts for workflow automation","Parsing Markdown guides for development workflow"],"zh":["初始化AI开发会话","执行Bash脚本以实现工作流自动化","解析Markdown指南以用于开发工作流"],"ja":["AI開発セッションの初期化","ワークフロー自動化のためのBashスクリプトの実行","開発ワークフローに使用するためのMarkdownガイドの解析"],"ko":["AI 개발 세션 초기화","워크플로우 자동화를 위한 Bash 스크립트 실행","개발 워크플로우에 사용되는 Markdown 가이드 파싱"],"es":["Inicialización de sesiones de desarrollo de IA","Ejecución de scripts de Bash para la automatización del flujo de trabajo","Análisis de guías de Markdown para el flujo de trabajo de desarrollo"],"fr":["Initialisation de sessions de développement d''IA","Exécution de scripts Bash pour l''automatisation du workflow","Analyse de guides Markdown pour le workflow de développement"],"de":["Initialisierung von AI-Entwicklungssitzungen","Ausführung von Bash-Skripten für die Workflow-Automatisierung","Analyse von Markdown-Leitfäden für den Entwicklungswerkfluss"],"pt":["Inicializando sessões de desenvolvimento de IA","Executando scripts Bash para automação de fluxo de trabalho","Analysando guias Markdown para fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Инициализация сессий разработки ИИ","Выполнение скриптов Bash для автоматизации рабочего процесса","Парсинг руководств Markdown для рабочего процесса разработки"],"ar":["تهيئة جلسات تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","تشغيل سكريبتات Bash للتحكم الآلي في تدفق العمل","تحليل دلائل Markdown لتدفق عمل التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to .trellis/workflow.md file","Bash script execution capabilities needed"],"zh":["需要访问.trellis/workflow.md文件","需要Bash脚本执行能力"],"ja":[".trellis/workflow.mdファイルへのアクセスが必要","Bashスクリプトの実行機能が必要"],"ko":[".trellis/workflow.md 파일에 접근할 수 있어야 합니다","Bash 스크립트 실행 기능이 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo .trellis/workflow.md","Se necesitan capacidades de ejecución de scripts de Bash"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au fichier .trellis/workflow.md","Des capacités d''exécution de scripts Bash sont nécessaires"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Datei .trellis/workflow.md","Bash-Skript-Ausführungsfähigkeiten sind erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo .trellis/workflow.md","Capacidades de execução de scripts Bash necessárias"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к файлу .trellis/workflow.md","Необходимы возможности выполнения скриптов Bash"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملف .trellis/workflow.md","يحتاج إلى إمكانيات تشغيل سكريبتات Bash"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"6ab8be66e77e5b13845bcf0610df8c12cebca1dc802f2f5d47562177be991ffb","qualityScore":50}');
